+# Score Easy — Audit Findings
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Score Easy is in solid shape on its foundations and shaky on its seams. The **production build passes** (exit 0) and the **402 unit tests across 44 files all pass**. The pure scoring math that is tested — sets win rules (`quickMatchSets`), cricket run-rate/NRR/points-table, tennis point ladder, round-robin generation, standings — is correct. The defects cluster precisely where tests do *not* reach: **component-level gating logic in the five live-scoring engines** (none of `Mono*LiveScore.jsx` has a direct test), the **derived statistics layer**, **persistence seams**, **cloud-sync recovery**, and the **half-finished green design migration**.
+
+Three themes dominate:
+
+1. **Two engines per sport that disagree.** Sets and goals each have a quick-match scorer and a separate tournament scorer with divergent completion logic. Single-set games end on a 1-point margin (win-by-2 not enforced), badminton tournament games can't complete at the 30 cap, and a tied no-draw goals match (e.g. basketball) auto-saves `winner: 'draw'` — corrupting standings and knockout brackets.
+2. **The functional app never got the green redesign.** The `#0066ff` blue the design system declared "dead" survives in 106 occurrences across 19 production files — every live scorer, the signed-in dashboard, history, statistics, tournaments, onboarding.
+3. **Local-first is solid; cloud/deploy resilience is not.** No local data is lost, but matches finished offline never backfill to the cloud, failed syncs are unrecoverable once you leave the result screen, and timed matches drift because the timer counts foreground ticks instead of wall-clock.
+
+No issue causes silent **local** data loss in normal play. The highest-impact correctness bugs are the cricket test-match 3rd-innings guard (makes the 4-innings format unplayable), the no-draw-goals auto-draw, the tennis-tournament data-shape mismatch (empty standings), and the single-set win-by-2 failure.
+
+### Totals by severity (deduped, false-positives removed)
+
+| Severity | Count |
+|----------|-------|
+| Critical (P0) | 7 |
+| High (P1) | 21 |
+| Medium (P2) | 28 |
+| Low (P3) | 33 |
+
+### Counts by category
+
+| Category | Count |
+|----------|-------|
+| Functionality & scoring correctness | 24 |
+| Navigation & page-to-page | 6 |
+| UX/UI | 13 |
+| Accessibility | 3 |
+| Performance | 7 |
+| Persistence & data | 10 |
+| Auth & onboarding | 7 |
+| Tournaments | 9 |
+| Mobile / Android (Capacitor) | 7 |
+| Offline / PWA | 7 |
+| Stats & history | 11 |
+| Error handling | 5 |
+
+Verification note: of the high/critical findings sent to verifiers, **5 were confirmed** (some severity-adjusted) and **1 was rejected** as a false-positive (`offline-pwa-no-update-ux` — the auto-reload path exists; see appendix). Severities below reflect verifier adjustments where applicable.
+
+> ⚠️ **The automated verify pass was mostly lost to a transient rate-limit.** A separate **lead re-check of all 7 P0s** (see "Lead verification addendum" at the end) confirmed **3** as true criticals (P0-1/3/4), found **P0-2 to be a false-positive** (the auto-end paths *are* guarded), and reclassified **P0-5→High**, **P0-6→Medium**, **P0-7→P1/P2**. So the **real P0 count is 3**, not 7. P1/P2 items below carried finder self-assessed "Confirmed" labels and were re-verified in a second pass (see addendum).
+
+> 📉 **Coverage gaps (be honest about these):** The dedicated **accessibility** and **navigation-routing** finder agents failed on *both* workflow runs (rate-limit / socket errors), and 5 per-sport agents (volleyball, badminton, squash, football, basketball) failed on the final run. So: **Accessibility is under-audited** — the only a11y findings (P3-14/15/16) are incidental catches from other agents, not a systematic pass; assume more exists. **Navigation** is reconstructed from the other agents' reports plus hands-on runtime testing, not a dedicated sweep. The 5 missing per-sport configs are largely covered by the shared **engine** reports (which all completed) and by runtime testing (volleyball/football/basketball were driven live), but sport-specific config nits for those five may be under-reported. **Mobile/Android is code-audited only** — no APK/emulator run; all native-behaviour items need on-device confirmation.
+
