+
+## Prioritized issues
+
+### P0 — Critical
+
+#### P0-1 · Cricket test match: 3rd innings ends on the first scoring stroke when the third-batting side already leads
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** Cricket (Test format) — `/:sport/quick/test-match/:matchId`
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:192-207` (`checkResult` guards only `currentInningsIndex < 2`), called from `addRuns` (274-276), `addWicket` (311), `addExtra` (334).
+- **User impact:** In the common case (team 1 leads after two innings, declines/ineligible for follow-on, bats again), the very first run makes `battingTotal > bowlingTotal` and the match is declared "Won by N runs" — innings 3 and 4 are skipped entirely. The 4-innings format is unplayable, and there is **no Undo on the match-complete screen**, so the wrong result can only be saved or the whole match discarded.
+- **Suggested direction:** Change the early-return to `if (currentInningsIndex < 3) return false;` so only the 4th innings can end the match mid-innings; route 3rd-innings completion through `advanceInnings`.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static trace; no test exists for this component).
+
+#### P0-2 · Timed no-draw goals match (e.g. basketball) auto-saves `winner: 'draw'`, corrupting standings and knockout brackets
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness / Tournaments
+- **Affected:** All goals sports with `drawAllowed:false` — basketball (`sportRegistry.js:222`) and at least one other (`:429`); both quick and tournament timed/points modes.
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:137-153` (timed auto-end) and `:222-237` (points auto-end) call `winner: determineWinner(...)`; `determineWinner` (`:17-21`) returns `'draw'` on equal scores with no `drawAllowed` check. The guard exists only in manual `saveMatch` (`:325`). Downstream: `knockoutManager.js:65-75` seeds the final from `semi.winner` = `'draw'`; `getTournamentWinner` (`:118-126`) then returns `null`/"Unknown"; standings count the game as played with no W/D/L (`standingsCalculator.js:139-148`).
+- **User impact:** A basketball match (naturally timed, frequently tied at the buzzer) is recorded as a "Draw" — a result the sport can't have. In a playoff, the bracket advances a phantom `'draw'` team, producing an unresolvable final between "Unknown" and a real team.
+- **Suggested direction:** Apply the `saveMatch` no-draw guard to both auto-end paths; prompt for OT/shootout or block the tied auto-finish; never persist `winner:'draw'` when `drawAllowed===false`. (Reported independently by the goals-engine and tournament audits — merged.)
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static trace; corroborated by `standingsCalculator.test.js:270-281`).
+
+#### P0-3 · Single-set games end on a 1-point margin — win-by-2 not enforced
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** All sets sports in single-set quick mode — volleyball, badminton, table tennis, pickleball, squash.
+- **Evidence:** `src/utils/volleyballCalculations.js:13-21` (`validateSingleSetScore`), consumed at `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1034,1139`. Verified empirically: `validateSingleSetScore(25,24,25) === true`, `(11,10,11) === true`. The match auto-finalizes the instant this returns true (`finalizeMatch`, `:642`).
+- **User impact:** A single set to 25 ends at **25-24**, directly contradicting the on-screen "Win by 2 at deuce" text (`:2628-2630`). Wrong, user-visible, unrecoverable result. Note: `volleyballCalculations.test.js:90` actively asserts the buggy `(11,10)===true` as expected — the test locks in the bug.
+- **Suggested direction:** Enforce `max - min >= winBy` (winBy from config, default 2) mirroring `quickMatchSets.isSetComplete`; fix the test.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (empirical replay in report).
+
+#### P0-4 · Tennis tournament sets persist as `games1/games2` but standings/UI read `score1/score2` — standings stay empty, scores blank
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness / Tournaments
+- **Affected:** Tennis tournaments.
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:56-67` (`makeBlankSet` has no `score1/score2`), `:522-534` (tournament `saveMatch` persists `sets` raw). Consumers read `score1/score2`: `standingsCalculator.js:42-50`, `GenericSetsTournament.jsx:34-35,242-243,316,321,329-331`.
+- **User impact:** Every set comparison is `undefined > undefined` → false, so both teams register 0 sets won, no W/L/points accrue, and per-set cells render `undefined-undefined`. A tennis tournament's league table stays empty no matter how many matches are played. The match `winner` is still saved correctly (computed from games/tiebreak), so it's a standings+display break, not a result break. The quick path is fine (`mapTennisSetsForQuickHistory` translates the shape).
+- **Suggested direction:** Have the tennis tournament save emit the shared `score1/score2` contract (mirror `mapTennisSetsForQuickHistory`), folding in the tiebreak 7-6 fix (P1-9).
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static; standings tests only feed volleyball-shaped sets, so the suite is silent here).
+
+#### P0-5 · No-ball / wide always adds exactly +1 — runs off the delivery are unrecordable
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** Cricket (limited-overs).
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:279-300` (`addExtra` hardcodes `runs + 1`); buttons labelled `Wide (+1)` / `No Ball (+1)` (`:761-768`).
+- **User impact:** Every boundary or running pair off a no-ball/wide is under-counted by up to 6 runs. On a free hit (only arises from a no-ball), a 4 or 6 can only be entered as +1, then a numbered run button that *consumes a legal ball that should not have been bowled*. Wrong team totals → wrong chases and NRR. A user watching a real over sees the score diverge from reality.
+- **Suggested direction:** Allow a follow-up run entry (extra +1 plus runs off the bat) without consuming a legal ball, or provide "No-ball + N" inputs.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static; no test for this component).
+
+#### P0-6 · Free hit is silently lost on a normal "Wicket" press — `addWicket` ignores `freeHit`
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** Cricket (limited-overs).
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:242-276` (`addWicket` unconditionally `team.wickets += 1`); the button at `:771-775` reads `Run Out Only` on a free hit but calls the same `addWicket`.
+- **User impact:** On a free hit (where only a run-out is legal) the button records a full, illegal dismissal — and if it's the last wicket, declares the side all-out / ends the innings. Corrupts wickets, all-out detection, and the win-by-wickets margin.
+- **Suggested direction:** On `freeHit`, allow only a run-out wicket; otherwise make the press a no-op while keeping the free hit live.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static).
+
+#### P0-7 · Corrupt or wrong-shaped list value crashes History, Dashboard, and Statistics with no in-app recovery
+- **Category:** Persistence & data / Error handling
+- **Affected:** History, Dashboard, Statistics screens (all contexts).
+- **Evidence:** `src/utils/storage.js:142-150` (`loadData` falls back to default only on `JSON.parse` throw/`null`, not on shape); array-assuming consumers `storage.js:243` (`matches.findIndex`), `MonoHistory.jsx:249-250`, `DashboardLanding.jsx:864-866`, `MonoStatistics.jsx:225-226`. Empirically: a non-array JSON value in `se_quickmatches` makes `.sort`/`.filter`/`.findIndex` throw.
+- **User impact:** Any valid-JSON-but-non-array value (schema drift, partial corruption, extension, future writer) crashes all three screens on open. Because the "Clear local history" recovery control lives *on* the History screen (`MonoHistory.jsx:459-472`), the only in-app remedy is unreachable — a soft-lock. Trigger likelihood is low (internal writers always produce arrays), but blast radius is total, hence P0.
+- **Suggested direction:** In `loadData`, coerce to the default's type (return default when `defaultValue` is an array and the parsed value is not); optionally quarantine the bad value.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (empirical in report).
+
+---
+
+### P1 — High
+
+#### P1-1 · Live match timer counts only foreground ticks — timed matches auto-end at the wrong wall-clock time
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness / Performance / Mobile
+- **Affected:** All timed goals sports (football, basketball, hockey, handball, futsal, kabaddi, rugby), quick and tournament.
+- **Evidence:** `src/hooks/useTimer.js:40-55` increments `elapsed` purely by counting `setInterval` ticks with no `Date.now()` anchor and no `visibilitychange` handler. Consumed for auto-end/countdown at `MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:137,151,213,440`. The resume path already reconstructs from wall-clock (`getRestoredTimerElapsed`, `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:215-221`) — the pattern is known but not applied to the live tick.
+- **User impact:** On mobile (Capacitor WebView), JS intervals are throttled when backgrounded and suspended on screen lock. A 10-minute timed match left locked for 3 minutes runs ~13 real minutes before auto-ending; the countdown freezes while backgrounded. Screen auto-lock during a live match is routine. (The auto-saved draft also omits `elapsed`, so a resumed timed match restarts the clock from 0 — see P1-2.)
+- **Suggested direction:** Anchor `elapsed` to a `startedAt` epoch and reconcile on each tick and on `visibilitychange`, reusing `getRestoredTimerElapsed`.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (verifier; "minor foreground skew, substantive defect is background/lock suspension").
+
+#### P1-2 · In-progress tournament scoring isn't persisted per point and has no flush-on-background (data-loss window)
+- **Category:** Mobile / Android (Capacitor) / Persistence
+- **Affected:** All five tournament scorers (Sets, Goals, Cricket, CricketTest, Tennis). CricketTest also has the same gap in its dedicated route (P1-3).
+- **Evidence:** `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:193` (`addPoint` mutates React state, writes nothing to storage); only `saveDraft()` (`:294→:311`) and match-completion persist. No autosave effect, no `setInterval`. The native flush hook `src/mobile/lifecycle.js:4` (`addAppStateChangeListener`) is **never imported anywhere in `src/`** — built but unwired. No `beforeunload`/`visibilitychange`/`pagehide` handler either. Quick Match is NOT affected (it autosaves every point).
+- **User impact:** On Android, a background transition (call, notification, app-switch) or a recents-swipe kills the WebView; all points scored since the last manual "Save Draft" are lost silently. A user has no reason to tap Save Draft mid-match.
+- **Suggested direction:** Add a debounced score-change autosave to the tournament engines, and/or wire `addAppStateChangeListener` at app root to flush the active draft on `isActive === false`.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (verifier; systemic across all five Mono*LiveScore components).
+
+#### P1-3 · Cricket test match has no auto-persistence — an unpaused long match is wiped on reload
+- **Category:** Persistence & data / Functionality
+- **Affected:** Cricket (Test) — the longest-running scoring flow.
+- **Evidence:** `MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:76-137` restores only from `draftState`; the sole writer is `saveDraft` (`:393-425`), invoked only by the **Pause** button, which renders only when `hasChanges` is true (`:799-808`). No change-driven persistence effect.
+- **User impact:** A reload, tab crash, OS kill, or backgrounding before Pause loses the entire match; the loader finds no `draftState` and reinitializes to 0/0. Highest-probability data-loss path in the app for the test format specifically.
+- **Suggested direction:** Debounced auto-save of `innings`/`currentInningsIndex`/`followOnEnforced` to `draftState` on change; surface the storage-full warning on failure.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static; overlaps P1-2 but distinct route/component).
+
+#### P1-4 · OnboardingGuard `isLoading` spinner can strand the whole web app (incl. guests) when Convex is unreachable
+- **Category:** Auth & onboarding / Error handling
+- **Affected:** Web (desktop + mobile-web), signed-in and guest, in cloud mode.
+- **Evidence:** `index.jsx:193` (`if (isLoading) return <LazyFallback/>` wrapping all routes 1203-1248); `CloudAuthProvider.jsx:127-132` (`isLoading` stays true while `isConvexAuthLoading` or `convexUser === undefined`); `main.jsx:182-183` (cloud mode never re-evaluates); `:175` (offline probe is native-only).
+- **User impact:** During a Convex outage or flaky connectivity at load, `isLoading` never flips, and there is no web cloud→local downgrade or timeout — the app is stuck on an infinite spinner. A brand-new guest who never intended to sign in can't reach local scoring at all, defeating the offline value proposition.
+- **Suggested direction:** Bound the `isLoading` gate with a timeout that falls through to a degraded local/OfflineFallback experience; never block unauthenticated routes on Convex connectivity.
+- **Verification:** Needs-runtime (logic path clear; exact websocket-stall behavior under hard-offline not reproduced).
+
+#### P1-5 · No sign-out control is rendered anywhere in the signed-in UI
+- **Category:** Auth & onboarding
+- **Affected:** All signed-in contexts.
+- **Evidence:** `AuthUserButton` is exported (`components/AuthButtons.jsx:88-100`) but a grep for `AuthUserButton|UserButton|SignOutButton|signOut|useClerk` across `src/` (excluding the definition + tests) returns **zero render sites**. `MonoProfile.jsx` has no sign-out; `GlobalNavigation` only links to `/profile`.
+- **User impact:** A signed-in user cannot sign out (shared device, account switch) without clearing site data or using Clerk's hosted pages. A core account flow is effectively missing.
+- **Suggested direction:** Mount `AuthUserButton` (or a custom `useClerk().signOut`) in `GlobalNavigation` and/or `MonoProfile`; `afterSignOutUrl="/"` is already configured.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (grep-verified absence).
+
+#### P1-6 · Cricket points-table tie-break is points→NRR only; ties seed the bracket non-deterministically and ignore wins/head-to-head
+- **Category:** Tournaments / Functionality
+- **Affected:** Cricket tournaments (esp. `winnerMode: 'table-topper'`).
+- **Evidence:** `src/utils/cricketCalculations.js:348-351` sorts only by `points` then `nrr`; the sorted table feeds `generateKnockoutMatches` which seeds 1v4 / 2v3 by index (`roundRobin.js:80-99`).
+- **User impact:** Two teams level on points and NRR (common with few matches) fall back to `Array.prototype.sort` order — no sporting tiebreak, not guaranteed stable. That order decides seeding and, in table-topper mode, the champion. Users perceive a wrong/arbitrary result.
+- **Suggested direction:** Extend the comparator with wins → head-to-head → NRR → stable fallback (team name).
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static).
+
+#### P1-7 · Editing/clearing a group match after the knockout stage starts leaves the bracket seeded from stale standings
+- **Category:** Tournaments
+- **Affected:** All three tournament engines.
+- **Evidence:** `knockoutManager.js:18-29` (`initializeKnockoutStage` early-returns once KO matches exist); phase-transition effects bail when KO exists (`GenericSetsTournament.jsx:70-85`, `GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:46-61`, `MonoCricketTournament.jsx:187-202`); `updateKnockoutBracket` (`knockoutManager.js:36-85`) re-seeds only from completed semis, never re-reads group standings. The "Clear" control renders on completed group matches regardless of `phase`.
+- **User impact:** After the bracket is generated, correcting a group score recomputes standings but the frozen KO seeds don't change — the wrong teams play the semis/final, silently.
+- **Suggested direction:** Disable group-match Clear/edit once `phase === 'knockout'`, or re-seed pending KO matches on group-result change; at minimum warn the user.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static).
+
+#### P1-8 · Cricket test match: follow-on innings victory is mislabeled "Won by N wickets" and spins up a phantom 4th innings
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** Cricket (Test) with enforced follow-on.
+- **Evidence:** `MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:210-232` (`advanceInnings`); innings-victory logic in `buildTestWinResult` (`cricketCalculations.js:195-208`) is only reached when `nextIndex >= 4`. End of innings 3 computes `nextIndex = 3 (<4)`, so it advances to a 4th innings instead; `checkResult` then fires on the first stroke → "Won by N wickets."
+- **User impact:** A genuine innings victory after a follow-on reports the wrong result type/margin and starts a meaningless extra innings. (Compounds P0-1.)
+- **Suggested direction:** In `advanceInnings`, detect the innings-victory/completed-match condition when the trailing side finishes its 2nd innings still behind, before advancing to index 3; reuse `countPlayedInnings`.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (static).
+
+#### P1-9 · Tiebreak-won tennis set never updates games to 7-6 (live row and stored history show 6-6)
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness
+- **Affected:** Tennis (quick + tournament).
+- **Evidence:** `MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:155-168` (`processTiebreakPoint` increments only `tiebreakPoints`, marks `completed`, never bumps `games`); display `:708-710` renders `6-6 (7-5)`. Quick history copies `score1=games1=6, score2=games2=6` (`tennisQuickMatch.js:12-15`) → a completed set looks like a 6-6 draw.
+- **User impact:** Tiebreak sets display as the non-standard `6-6` and a games-derived winner inference reads them as a tie. Match winner/sets tally are unaffected (computed from `tiebreakPoints`), but it compounds P0-4 (a remapped 6-6 set is still a tie in standings).
+- **Suggested direction:** On tiebreak completion, award the winning side the 7th game (set 7-6) before marking complete.
+- **Verification:** Confirmed (replay in report).
+
+#### P1-10 · Tennis match-clinch advances `currentSet` into a phantom empty set; the dead score pad looks live
+- **Category:** Functionality & scoring correctness / UX
+- **Affected:** Tennis (best-of-3 / best-of-5 decided early).
+- **Evidence:** `MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:357-359` (`advanceFn` advances whenever `setIdx < totalSets-1`, no match-complete check); `isMatchComplete` (`:334-339`) is already true. After clinching, `currentSet` points at an empty `makeBlankSet()`; the pad reads from `sets[2]` (`:556`) showing 0/0, the badge says "Set 3 of 3" beside "Match Complete," and `canScoreCurrentSet` (`:569`) is true so the pad renders live/clickable but taps are swallowed (`:348`).
+- **User impact:** Confusing end-of-match state — an enabled-looking score pad that does nothing, contradictory "Set 3 of 3" + "Match Complete." Saved result is correct.
+- **Suggested direction:** Stop advancing once `isMatchComplete` would be true; keep `currentSet` on the decider.
