+## Dropped false-positives (appendix)
+
+- **`offline-pwa-no-update-ux`** — *Rejected by verifier.* Claimed there is no reload UX after a deploy, but the cited line numbers were stale. The actual SW registration in `registerWebServiceWorker()` (`src/main.jsx:158-173`) adds a one-shot `controllerchange` listener that calls `location.reload()` (guarded by `SW_CONTROLLER_RELOAD_KEY`) and calls `registration.update()`; the built `dist/sw.js` contains `skipWaiting` + `cleanupOutdatedCaches`. The reload fires at SW takeover before the user can navigate to a not-yet-loaded lazy route, so orphaned chunks aren't requested. A route-level `ErrorBoundary` (`index.jsx:1201-1202`) is a secondary defense. The "no reload prompt" premise is false; residual (no in-place chunk-retry, only hard reload) is industry-standard. Adjusted to low and removed from the main list.
