+## Lead verification addendum — independent re-check of the 7 P0 criticals
+
+The automated verify pass was largely lost to a transient server-side rate-limit (only ~12 of 56 high/critical findings got an independent verdict). So the lead re-read the cited code for **all 7 P0s** directly. Result: **4 are solid criticals, 1 is real but should be High, and 2 are over-severity.**
+
+| ID | Verdict | Notes |
+|----|---------|-------|
+| **P0-1** Cricket test 3rd-innings premature end | ✅ **Confirmed — Critical** | `MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:211` guards `currentInningsIndex < 2`; from innings 3 on, the match ends the instant `battingTotal > bowlingTotal`. Verified: T1 200 / T2 150 → T1's first run in innings 3 = 201 > 150 → "Won". 4-innings format is unplayable. Fix: `< 3`. |
+| **P0-2** No-draw goals auto-saves `winner:'draw'` | ❌ **False-positive** (tournament path) | Deeper read: `determineWinner` (`:25-29`) does return `'draw'` in isolation, **but all 3 completion paths are guarded**. Timed auto-end (`:152-162`) and manual-end (`:342-348`) call `getBasketballCompletionState({drawAllowed})` → on a tie in a no-draw sport `canComplete` is false → **overtime**, no save. Points-mode auto-end (`:252-264`) only fires when `newScore >= target`, i.e. the scoring team is *ahead* — it cannot be tied at completion. So no completion path persists `winner:'draw'` for a no-draw sport. Finder's cited lines (137-153/222-237) were wrong and missed the `getBasketballCompletionState` guard. (The `MonoQuickMatch` goals path wasn't separately re-verified, but the bracket-corruption impact is tournament-only, and the tournament scorer is guarded.) |
+| **P0-3** Single-set win-by-2 not enforced | ✅ **Confirmed — Critical** | `volleyballCalculations.js:13-21` `validateSingleSetScore(25,24,25)===true` (deuce branch only triggers when `min>=target`); multi-set `validateSetScore` *does* enforce win-by-2. Worse: `volleyballCalculations.test.js:90` asserts `(11,10)===true`, **locking the bug into the test suite**. Contradicts on-screen "Win by 2". |
+| **P0-4** Tennis tournament set-shape mismatch | ✅ **Confirmed — Critical** | `MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:63-67` `makeBlankSet` is `{games1,games2,points1,points2}` — **no `score1/score2`** (those exist only in display helpers, :215-220). Tournament save persists raw sets; `standingsCalculator`/`GenericSetsTournament` read `score1/score2` → `undefined` → empty standings. (Match `winner` still correct.) |
+| **P0-5** Cricket no-ball/wide always +1 | ⚠️ **Confirmed mechanism — downgrade to High** | `MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:292` hardcodes `runs + 1`; runs off the delivery are unrecordable. Real correctness gap, but most wides/no-balls are genuinely +1 in casual scoring — **High**, not Critical. |
+| **P0-6** Free hit lost on "Wicket" press | ❌ **Over-severity — downgrade to Medium** | `addWicket` (:241-275) clears `freeHit` and increments wickets — but on a free hit a **run-out is legal and *should* count**, and the button is already relabeled "Run Out Only" (:771). The real gap is *non-enforcement* (a non-run-out could be mis-entered), not a silent wrong result. **Medium.** |
+| **P0-7** Corrupt list value crashes History/Stats | ⚠️ **Over-severity — downgrade to P1/P2** | Real `loadData` is `storage.js:276-284` (the finding cited `:142-150` — wrong), and returns parsed JSON without shape-coercion. **But** `normalizedQuickMatches` guards `!Array.isArray → []` (`:157`), and the finding itself rates the trigger low-likelihood. Defensive-coding gap, blast radius real but trigger unlikely → **P1/P2**, not P0. |
+
+**Net:** true P0 count is **3** (P0-1, P0-3, P0-4). **P0-2 → false-positive** (guarded). P0-5 → P1 (High). P0-6 → P2 (Medium). P0-7 → P1/P2 (robustness). The three confirmed criticals are all in **untested live-scorer component logic**, consistent with the green unit suite. **Methodological note:** of 7 finder-"confirmed" P0s, the lead re-check found 1 false-positive, 2 over-severity, and 1 borderline — a ~57% adjustment rate. This is why the P1 tier was independently re-verified (next section) rather than shipped on finder labels. A recurring failure mode in the finder reports: **cited line numbers drift from the actual code** (seen in P0-2, P0-7), so always confirm against the current file before fixing.
