+
+**Bottom line after both verification passes:** the audit's *true* high-impact set is small and concrete — **P0-1** (cricket test 3rd-innings), **P0-3** (single-set win-by-2 + a test locking the bug), **P0-4** (tennis tournament standings empty), and **P1-7** (stale knockout bracket). P0-5 (cricket extras +1) is a solid High. Everything above P2 should be re-confirmed against current line numbers before work begins — the finder line refs drift and severities skew high. The remaining medium/low items are still worth fixing but are not the emergencies the raw finder labels implied.
+
+The four confirmed false-positives in the **in-progress-draft cluster** (P1-2, P1-3, P1-19, P1-5) share one root cause worth internalizing: the app already has robust **per-point autosave + status-gated reads + draft-key separation**, and the finders missed it by reading stale/pre-refactor line numbers. Treat any remaining finding about "draft persistence / in-progress pollution / no autosave" with the same skepticism.
+
+> **Scrutiny asymmetry — weight the tiers accordingly.** The **P0** verdicts were *lead-verified by reading the code directly*. The **P1** verdicts are *agent-produced* (one level less scrutiny) — and the two automated passes openly **disagreed** on P1-1 and P1-2 (pass 1 said "confirmed high"; the deeper pass 2, citing the autosave effect + a green test, said medium / false-positive). Where they conflict, this doc trusts the evidence-cited deeper verdict, but a human should spot-read P1 items before fixing. P2/P3 carry only finder self-assessment and are the **least** scrutinized.
+
+> **Accessibility is an under-covered explicit ask.** You asked about "the different ways a user could be experiencing this" — screen-reader and keyboard-only use is squarely that, and it is the audit's thinnest layer (both dedicated a11y agents died on both runs; P3-14/15/16 are incidental catches). The tennis scorer's keyboard shortcuts + aria-live are a good sign, but the scoring loop, setup forms, dialogs, and color-contrast were not systematically tested with assistive tech. **Recommend a single focused accessibility pass** (axe/Lighthouse + keyboard-only + screen-reader walkthrough of score→save→history) as a follow-up — say the word and I'll run it.
