+## Summary
+
+The auth stack (Clerk + Convex behind a `cloud`/`local` bootstrap switch) is generally well-structured: returnTo handling is XSS-safe, onboarding deferral lets guests keep scoring, and `cloudAuthAvailable` gating cleanly hides cloud-only UI when env vars are missing. However, tracing real journeys surfaced two serious gaps: on **web**, a single `isLoading` chokepoint in `OnboardingGuard` can strand the entire app (including guests scoring locally) on a permanent spinner when Convex is unreachable, and there is **no sign-out control rendered anywhere** in the signed-in UI. Several medium/low UX and continuity issues round out the list.
+
+Severity tally: **critical 1, high 1, medium 3, low 4** (9 findings).
+
+Note on verified-safe items: native `pk_live` host gating is NOT a bug — `capacitor.config.ts` sets `server.hostname: 'scoreeasy.app'`, so the native WebView origin satisfies `isAllowedProductionHost` (bootstrap.js:14-16) and cloud auth works on Android/iOS.
+
+---
+
+### [CRITICAL] OnboardingGuard `isLoading` spinner can strand the whole web app (incl. guests) when Convex is unreachable
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:193` (`if (isLoading) return <LazyFallback />;` wrapping the entire `<Routes>` tree at lines 1203-1248); `src/auth/CloudAuthProvider.jsx:127-132` (`isLoading = isConvexAuthLoading || !isClerkLoaded || (isAuthenticated && (convexUser === undefined …))`); `src/main.jsx:182-183` (once `mode==='cloud'`, `updateAuthBootstrap` returns early and never re-evaluates); `src/main.jsx:175` (the offline-escape native probe is gated on `isNativeRuntime()`, so web never probes).
+- **What's wrong:** In cloud mode, `OnboardingGuard` renders a spinner in front of *every* route — guest landing, local scoring, history — whenever `useAuth().isLoading` is true. `isLoading` stays true while the Convex auth websocket is connecting (`isConvexAuthLoading`) or `convexUser === undefined`. If Convex is unreachable (backend outage, or the web user is offline at initial load), `useConvexAuth` never resolves and `convexUser` never arrives, so `isLoading` never flips to false. On web there is no cloud→local downgrade (main.jsx:182 short-circuits) and no native-style probe/timeout, so the app is stuck on `<AppLoading compact />` forever.
+- **User impact:** A user (including a brand-new guest who never intended to sign in) opening the app during a Convex outage or with flaky connectivity sees an infinite loading spinner and cannot reach guest local scoring at all — the core offline value proposition is blocked. Desktop browser and mobile-web; signed-in and guest both affected.
+- **Suggested direction:** Add a bounded timeout/fallback to the `isLoading` gate (e.g. after N seconds of `isConvexAuthLoading`, fall through to a degraded local experience or render an OfflineFallback-style recovery), and/or don't block unauthenticated routes on Convex connection state. Guest routes should never depend on Convex being reachable.
+- **Confidence:** medium (logic path is clear; exact websocket-stall behavior of `useConvexAuth` under hard-offline isn't reproduced here, but no timeout guard exists either way).
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] No sign-out control is rendered anywhere in the signed-in UI
+
+- **Evidence:** `AuthUserButton` is exported at `src/components/AuthButtons.jsx:88-100` but a grep for `AuthUserButton|UserButton|SignOutButton|signOut|useClerk` across `src/` (excluding `AuthButtons.jsx` and tests) returns **zero render sites**. `MonoProfile.jsx` (the `/profile` screen, full file read) contains no sign-out affordance; `GlobalNavigation` (index.jsx:409-414) only links Profile → `/profile`.
+- **What's wrong:** The Clerk `UserButton`/sign-out is implemented as a reusable component but never mounted. There is no path in the app for a signed-in user to sign out.
+- **User impact:** A signed-in user cannot sign out (e.g. on a shared device, or to switch accounts) without clearing site data / using Clerk's hosted pages directly. Sign-out is a core account flow and it is effectively missing. All contexts.
+- **Suggested direction:** Mount `AuthUserButton` (or a custom sign-out button using Clerk's `useClerk().signOut`) in `GlobalNavigation` and/or on `MonoProfile`. `afterSignOutUrl="/"` is already configured in `CloudAuthRoot.jsx:38`.
+- **Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Guest-scored matches are never migrated to the cloud account after sign-in
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/hooks/useMatchSync.js:91-124` (`syncMatch` only runs when `isAuthenticated`, and is invoked at save-time from the live scorers); there is no bulk migration of existing local `se_quickmatches` into Convex on first sign-in. Convex `save` is the only write path (`convex/matches.ts:66`). `CloudAuthProvider`/`store` (convex/users.ts:115-147) only upserts the user record, never imports local matches.
+- **What's wrong:** Matches a user scores as a guest (stored in localStorage under `se_` keys) are not uploaded when they later create an account. Only matches saved *while already authenticated* sync to the cloud profile/stats.
+- **User impact:** A returning guest with saved history who signs up expects their existing matches to appear on their profile and cloud stats; instead the cloud profile starts empty (local history still shows via DashboardLanding reading `se_quickmatches`, so data isn't lost, but it never reaches the account/profile/leaderboard). Possibly intended product behavior, but a likely surprise. All contexts.
+- **Suggested direction:** On first successful onboarding/sign-in, offer (or automatically perform) a one-time import of local matches into Convex via the existing `save` mutation, keyed by `clientMatchId` for idempotency.
+- **Confidence:** medium (could be a deliberate scope decision).
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] "Sign in" nav entry does not preserve the current page (returnTo lost)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:411-412` and `421` — the nav builds `{ label: 'Sign in', path: '/login' }` with no `returnTo` query and no `rememberAuthReturnTo(currentPath)` call before navigating. `MonoLogin`/`MonoSignUp` only read returnTo from the URL (`getAuthReturnToFromSearch`, MonoLogin.jsx:11-14), defaulting to `/`.
+- **What's wrong:** A signed-out user who clicks "Sign in" from `/history`, `/statistics`, or a sport setup page is sent to `/login` with no memory of where they were, so after auth they land on `/` instead of returning to the page they left.
+- **User impact:** Mild disorientation / extra navigation after signing in from a deep page. Desktop and mobile-web (nav + bottom nav).
+- **Suggested direction:** When the nav navigates to `/login`, pass `?returnTo=<current path>` (or call `rememberAuthReturnTo(getReturnTo(location))`) so post-auth redirect returns the user to where they were.
+- **Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] `SignedOut` ignores `isLoading`, unlike `SignedIn` (latent flash / inconsistency)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/components/AuthButtons.jsx:130-138` — `SignedOut` returns children whenever `!isAuthenticated`, with no `isLoading` check; `SignedIn` (lines 116-124) correctly gates on `isLoading`.
+- **What's wrong:** During the auth-loading window, `isAuthenticated` is false, so any `SignedOut` subtree renders even though auth state is unknown. Today this is masked on the landing page because `OnboardingGuard`'s `isLoading` spinner (index.jsx:193) prevents `MonoLanding` from mounting at all in cloud mode — so the guest-landing flash does not currently paint. But the asymmetry is a latent bug: any future `SignedOut` usage *outside* the guarded route tree (or if the guard's gate is relaxed per the critical finding) would flash guest content to a logged-in user.
+- **User impact:** None currently observable on the main flow; latent risk of guest UI flashing for authenticated users if `SignedOut` is reused elsewhere or the guard changes.
+- **Suggested direction:** Mirror `SignedIn` — have `SignedOut` render nothing while `isLoading` is true.
+- **Confidence:** high (code asymmetry verified; user-visible impact currently masked, hence medium not high).
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] StepName Clerk pre-fill effect has a stale/empty dependency array (name may not pre-fill)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoOnboarding.jsx:195-204` — the effect reads `clerkUser`, `firstName`, `lastName` but has `[]` deps, so it runs only once on mount. If `clerkUser` is still `null` on first render (Clerk hydrating asynchronously after a redirect-based OAuth sign-up), the pre-fill never re-runs when `clerkUser` arrives.
+- **What's wrong:** Google OAuth users may land on the Name step with empty first/last name fields even though Clerk has their name.
+- **User impact:** Minor — user retypes their name. Mitigated because `handleSubmit` falls back to `clerkUser?.firstName` at submit time (MonoOnboarding.jsx:784), so the stored record is still correct; the defect is cosmetic (empty input fields).
+- **Suggested direction:** Add `clerkUser` (and the relevant fields) to the dependency array, or initialize state from `clerkUser` once it loads.
+- **Confidence:** high (the cosmetic-only nature is confirmed by the submit-time fallback).
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Onboarding profanity/validation can be bypassed by client/server normalization mismatch on edge usernames
+
+- **Evidence:** Client `validateUsername` (MonoOnboarding.jsx:114-126) and server `validateUsernameValue` (convex/users.ts:67-83) duplicate the rules, but the consecutive-special-char regex differs in ordering and the client strips characters (`replaceAll(/[^a-z0-9_.]/g, "")`) before validating while the server only lowercases+trims. The two BLOCKED_WORDS lists are maintained separately (MonoOnboarding.jsx:47-92 vs convex/users.ts:25-57) and can drift.
+- **What's wrong:** Two independent copies of a security-relevant filter invite drift; the server list is the real gate but is easy to let fall behind the client.
+- **User impact:** Low — a username the client blocks could in principle be accepted by the server if the lists diverge, or vice-versa (confusing UX where the client says "available" but the server rejects). Not currently exploitable beyond cosmetic mismatch.
+- **Suggested direction:** Share a single source of truth for the word list / validation (or at minimum add a test asserting the two lists are identical). Server remains the authority.
+- **Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] `MonoProfile` own-profile-by-username still fires a redundant public query and shows reduced data
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoProfile.jsx:123-138` — when a signed-in user visits `/profile/<their-own-username>`, `isOwnProfile` is true (`displayUser = currentUser`), but `profileUser = useQuery(getByUsername, { username })` still runs, and the public-profile path uses `toPublicProfile` (convex/users.ts:105-113) which omits role/firstName etc.
+- **What's wrong:** Visiting your own profile via the username URL is treated partly as a public profile; a redundant query runs and some owner-only fields differ from the no-param `/profile` view.
+- **User impact:** Minor inconsistency between `/profile` and `/profile/<self>`; an extra network query. All cloud contexts.
+- **Suggested direction:** Skip the `getByUsername` query when `isOwnProfile`; render the same owner view for both URLs.
+- **Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] StepIndicator and onboarding selection chips still use the dead `#0066ff` blue
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoOnboarding.jsx:152,165,474,486,492,521,523,615,616,626` — hardcoded `#0066ff` / `#f0f6ff` accents in the progress bar, role cards, play-style chips, and sport tiles.
+- **What's wrong:** Per the project design system (green monotone via `var(--primary)`; "old `#0066ff` blue is dead"), the onboarding wizard never migrated to the current accent tokens.
+- **User impact:** Visual inconsistency — onboarding is blue-accented while the rest of the app is field-green. Polish only. All contexts.
+- **Suggested direction:** Replace hardcoded blue/`#f0f6ff` with `var(--primary)` / `var(--accent)` tokens.
+- **Confidence:** high.
