+# Navigation, routing & page-to-page transitions
+
+## Summary
+
+The route table in `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx` is well structured and the core
+journeys (landing -> play -> setup -> live -> result -> history/stats, and the tournament
+list -> setup -> bracket -> match flows) all resolve to real routes. The most significant
+issues cluster around one root cause: the scoring-exit / back-button protection keys purely
+off the URL path (`isProtectedScoringPath`, which matches any path segment `quick`), while the
+quick-match screen runs setup, live, and result as internal `phase` state under the *same*
+URL `/:sport/quick`. This produces (a) false "unsaved scoring progress may be lost" prompts on
+the setup form and on the already-saved result screen, and (b) stranded phantom history entries
+on every forward exit from a protected route, so pressing Back from the screen the user exited to
+silently drops them back into the abandoned scoring screen. A second cluster is dead legacy code
+(`MonoHome`, `MonoSetup`, `MonoLiveGame`, `MonoSportHome_TABBED`, and the `/game/:id` resume button)
+that navigates to routes which no longer exist; these are currently unreachable in the live flow
+but are latent traps.
+
+Severity tally: critical 0, high 2, medium 4, low 4.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Confirm-on-leave guard fires false "unsaved progress" warning on setup and result phases
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:154-163` (`isProtectedScoringPath` matches
+`segments.includes('quick')`); `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:273` (`phase` state =
+`setup | scoring | result`, all under the single URL `/:sport/quick`); `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:642-657`
+(`finalizeMatch` calls `persistQuickMatch` then `setPhase('result')` while the URL stays
+`/:sport/quick`); `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1364-1370` (`handleSetupBack` calls `navigate(-1)` on the
+team-setup step).
+
+**What's wrong:** Because the guard is path-only and all three phases share one URL, the
+"Leave this page? Your unsaved scoring progress may be lost." prompt fires:
+- on the **setup form**, before any score exists (e.g. user presses the in-app back arrow which
+  calls `navigate(-1)` at `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1366`, or the browser/native back, or the header
+  brand/menu via `go()` at `index.jsx:389-400`); and
+- on the **result screen**, after the match is already saved to history and the draft is cleared
+  (`finalizeMatch` persisted at `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:654-655`), so the warning is factually wrong —
+  there is no unsaved progress to lose.
+
+**User impact:** Users are warned about losing data that either does not exist yet (setup) or has
+already been saved (result). This trains users to ignore the dialog and undermines its value for the
+one case where it matters (mid-scoring). Affects every context (desktop, mobile-web, Android) since
+the guard and `phase` model are platform-independent.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Make the protection phase-aware rather than path-only — gate on an actual
+"dirty scoring in progress" signal (e.g. `phase === 'scoring'` / presence of an un-finalized draft)
+exposed to the guard, instead of matching the `quick` URL segment unconditionally.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Forward exit from a protected scoring route strands a phantom history entry; Back re-enters the abandoned scoring screen
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:1110-1114` (on entering a protected route the
+effect does `history.pushState({...state, gameProtection: true})` — a dummy entry);
+`index.jsx:1130-1161` (`leaveProtectedRouteAfterConfirm` is the *only* place the dummy entries are
+unwound, via `history.go(-backDelta)` on the back-confirm path); `index.jsx:389-400`
+(`GlobalNavigation.go` confirms then calls `navigate(path)` **forward**, never unwinding the dummy);
+result-screen buttons `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2802` (`/history`), `2805` (`/statistics`), `2815` (`/`)
+call `navigate()` directly; scoring->bracket exits `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:376`,
+`MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:161/245/356`, `MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:467`,
+`MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:488/490`, `MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:497/545`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Every *forward* `navigate()` away from a protected route leaves the dummy
+`gameProtection` history entry (whose URL is the scoring route) stranded one slot below the
+destination. When the destination screen mounts, it is not protected, so the effect tears down its
+`popstate` handler (`index.jsx:1096-1102`). If the user then presses Back, they land on the stranded
+dummy entry — the scoring URL — so the scoring component remounts, re-arms the guard, and a second
+Back press fires the false "unsaved progress" prompt. Trace (menu exit from `/cricket/quick`):
+`/play` -> `quick`(real) -> `dummy` -> push `/history`; Back from `/history` lands on `dummy`
+(= `/cricket/quick`) instead of `/play`.
+
+**User impact:** Back navigation after leaving a match (via header brand, hamburger menu, or any
+in-screen "View history / See stats / Home / back to bracket" button) does not return to the
+expected previous screen; it drops the user back into the match they just left and then shows a
+spurious data-loss prompt. Confusing on all platforms; especially bad on Android where Back is the
+primary navigation gesture. No actual data loss — the quick-match draft is persisted continuously
+(`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:473`) and cleared after finalize (`655`), which is why this is high, not critical.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Treat forward exits symmetrically with the back-confirm path — when leaving a
+protected route via `go()`/in-screen buttons, replace or pop the dummy `gameProtection` entry (e.g.
+`navigate(path, { replace: true })` from the scoring URL, or unwind the pushed dummies) so no
+scoring entry is left in the forward history.
+
+**Confidence:** medium (static history-stack trace; a single Back-press repro in a running build
+would raise it to high).
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] DashboardLanding "Resume" button navigates to non-existent `/game/:id` route
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/landing/DashboardLanding.jsx:576`
+(`onClick={() => navigate('/game/${session.id}')}`); `DashboardLanding.jsx:861`
+(`setSessions(getActiveSessions())`); `src/utils/universalStorage.js:47-49`
+(`getActiveSessions` returns sessions with status `active`/`paused` from key `gs_sessions`);
+the route table `index.jsx:1205-1246` has **no** `/game` route, so `/game/:id` falls through to
+`<Route path="*" element={<NotFoundRoute />}>`.
+
+**What's wrong:** The active-session "Resume" tile links to `/game/:id`, a route that does not exist.
+It renders only when `getActiveSessions()` is non-empty. In the current live flow this is effectively
+empty: the only writer of `gs_sessions` active sessions is `hooks/useGameSession.js:27` (`saveSession`),
+which is imported only by the dead `MonoSetup.jsx` and `MonoLiveGame.jsx` (no live importers — see
+Low finding below). The live quick-match screen (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx`) does not use
+`useGameSession`/`saveSession` at all, so it never populates active sessions.
+
+**User impact:** For a returning user who has stale `gs_sessions` from an older app version that *did*
+write active sessions, the dashboard shows a Resume card that lands on the "This screen is not
+available" Not Found page — a dead end on a prominent dashboard action. Signed-in/returning-with-data
+contexts only; new users and the current write path are unaffected.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Either remove the active-sessions block from `DashboardLanding` (it is fed by
+the dead session model), or repoint Resume to the live resume mechanism (the persisted
+`se_quickmatch_draft_*` draft restored by `MonoQuickMatch`), and/or add a migration that clears legacy
+`gs_sessions`.
+
+**Confidence:** high (route absence and data source verified); medium on real-world reachability
+(depends on stale legacy storage).
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Setup phase has no bottom-nav and only a back arrow that triggers the false guard
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:347`
+(`showBottomNav = !isProtectedScoringPath(pathname)`) hides the bottom nav on all of `/:sport/quick`;
+`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1364-1370` (`handleSetupBack` -> `navigate(-1)` on team step, else just steps the
+wizard back).
+
+**What's wrong:** On the quick-match **setup** screen the mobile bottom nav is hidden (because the URL
+is treated as a protected scoring path), so the only way out is the in-screen back arrow. On the first
+setup step that back arrow calls `navigate(-1)`, which the protected-route `popstate` guard intercepts
+and answers with the false "unsaved scoring progress may be lost" prompt (see first HIGH finding).
+
+**User impact:** A user who opens setup and changes their mind is funnelled through a data-loss warning
+to leave a form where nothing has been entered/scored, and has no bottom-nav alternative. Mobile-web
+and Android primarily.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Resolve via the phase-aware guard fix (first HIGH finding); optionally keep the
+bottom nav visible during the setup phase since no scoring is in progress there.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] `navigate` fired from a `setTimeout` after save can run after unmount
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:467`
+(`setTimeout(() => navigate('/${sport || 'cricket'}/tournament/${id}'), 300)`);
+`MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:32` (`navigateToTournament`). Similar deferred-navigation pattern is used by
+the back-guard fallback at `index.jsx:1155-1160`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Navigation to the bracket after a tournament cricket match is saved is deferred 300ms
+via `setTimeout` with no cleanup. If the component unmounts in that window (fast double-tap, app
+backgrounded on Android), the timer may call `navigate` on a stale closure. There is also a latent
+interaction risk with the back-guard's own 300ms fallback timeout (`index.jsx:1155`) if both fire
+around the same transition.
+
+**User impact:** Edge-case only: a possible no-op navigation or a transition that lands a beat late.
+Unlikely to corrupt state but can feel janky on slower devices.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Clear the timeout on unmount (store the id and clear in an effect cleanup) or
+navigate synchronously after the save resolves.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] `rematch` / sport-param navigation trusts `entry.sport` and can dead-end on unknown sports
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoHistory.jsx:434-441`
+(`navigate('/${entry.sport}/quick', { state: { teams } })`); `MonoHistory.jsx:700`
+(`navigate('/play?sport=${action.sportId}')`); `SportRouteGuard` at `index.jsx:91-95` renders
+`NotFoundRoute` when `getSportById(sport)` is falsy.
+
+**What's wrong:** Rematch and the history quick-actions build the target URL straight from stored
+`entry.sport` / `action.sportId`. If a history record carries a sport id that is not (or no longer) in
+`sportRegistry` (legacy data, renamed/removed sport), `/:sport/quick` is rejected by `SportRouteGuard`
+and the user lands on the Not Found page instead of a rematch. (`/play?sport=unknown` is softer:
+`MonoSportHome.jsx:688-713` simply ignores an unrecognised `?sport=` and shows the default picker.)
+
+**User impact:** Returning users with older history could hit a dead end when trying to rematch a saved
+result. Low likelihood but a broken core action when it occurs.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Validate `entry.sport` against `getSportById` before navigating in
+`rematchEntry`; fall back to `/play` (or the picker) with a toast if the sport is unknown.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Dead legacy screens navigate to removed `/game/:id` and `/setup` routes
+
+**Evidence:** `MonoHome.jsx:46/60` and `MonoSetup.jsx:62` navigate to `/setup`; `MonoHome.jsx:82`,
+`MonoSetup.jsx:49`, `MonoLiveGame.jsx:102`, `MonoSportHome_TABBED.jsx:156` navigate to `/setup` or
+`/game/:id`; verified none of `MonoHome`, `MonoSetup`, `MonoLiveGame`, `MonoSportHome_TABBED` is
+imported by any live component, and there is no `/game` or `/setup` route in `index.jsx:1205-1246`.
+
+**What's wrong:** These components reference routes that no longer exist, but they are dead code (no
+importers, not in the route tree). They only contribute confusion and bundle weight.
+
+**User impact:** None at runtime (unreachable). Maintenance/onboarding risk only.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Delete the unused `MonoHome.jsx`, `MonoSetup.jsx`, `MonoLiveGame.jsx`,
+`MonoSportHome_TABBED.jsx` (and the now-orphaned `hooks/useGameSession.js` if nothing else uses it).
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Dev-only landing-design showcases use raw `<a href>` for internal nav and one dead showcase link
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/landing-designs/LandingDesignA.jsx:177/199/202/360/363` and
+`landing-designs/BrutalistBlueVariants.jsx:204/232/239/395/402` use `<a href="/login|/play|/signup">`
+(full-page reload instead of SPA `<Link>`); `landing-designs/BrutalistColorShowcase.jsx:121`
+(`<a href="/showcase/landing-designs">`) points to a route that does not exist. All of these render
+only under `BrutalistColorShowcase`, reachable only when `SHOW_INTERNAL_ROUTES` is true
+(`index.jsx:47`, `1236-1243`).
+
+**What's wrong:** Raw anchors trigger a full document reload (losing SPA state), and the
+`/showcase/landing-designs` link is dead. These are gated to dev/internal builds.
+
+**User impact:** None in production (internal-routes flag off). Dev/demo only.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Switch internal showcases to `<Link>`/`navigate`, fix or remove the
+`/showcase/landing-designs` link, or drop the showcase variants if no longer used.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] `CloudAuthOnly` renders `null` for one frame before redirecting when cloud auth is unavailable
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/components/CloudAuthOnly.jsx:10-18` (redirect to `/` happens in
+`useEffect`; meanwhile the component returns `null`).
+
+**What's wrong:** When Convex/Clerk env is missing (`cloudAuthAvailable === false`) and a user lands on
+`/login`, `/signup`, `/profile`, `/onboarding`, etc. (e.g. via deep link or old bookmark), the screen
+renders blank for one render before the effect redirects home. Nav correctly hides the Profile/Sign in
+entries in this context (`index.jsx:409-414/420-422`), so this is only a transient flash on direct
+entry.
+
+**User impact:** Brief blank flash before redirect for the env-missing context (self-hosted / misconfig
+builds). No dead end.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Compute the redirect during render (e.g. return `<Navigate to="/" replace />`
+when `!cloudAuthAvailable`) instead of via effect, to avoid the empty frame.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Native back-button / scoring-exit fallback relies on a 300ms timing race for direct/deep-link entry
+
+**Evidence:** `index.jsx:1106-1108` (when entering a protected route at history index 0, the base index
+is set to `NO_PRIOR_ROUTE_INDEX`); `index.jsx:1146-1160` (the else branch does `history.back()` plus a
+`popstate` listener plus a 300ms `setTimeout` fallback that `navigate('/play', { replace: true })`).
+
+**What's wrong:** For a user who opens a scoring URL directly (deep link, refresh, shared link) with no
+prior in-app history, leaving after confirm depends on a `history.back()` either firing `popstate`
+within 300ms or the timeout firing. On a slow device or if `popstate` semantics differ, there is a
+narrow window for a double navigation or a slightly delayed exit. Functionally it resolves to `/play`,
+so it is robust, just timing-sensitive.
+
+**User impact:** Rare, edge-only; at worst a momentary delay or a redundant navigation when exiting a
+directly-opened scoring screen. Affects deep-link / refresh entry, notably Android (Capacitor) and
+shared web links.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Prefer an explicit `navigate('/play', { replace: true })` for the no-prior-route
+case rather than relying on `history.back()` + timeout, removing the timing dependency.
+
+**Confidence:** low.
