+# Offline & PWA behaviour
+
+## Summary
+
+Score Easy is genuinely offline-first for the thing that matters most — every match is written to `localStorage` *before* any cloud sync is attempted, so scoring continues and no local data is lost when the network drops. The real weaknesses are all on the **cloud-divergence** and **deploy-freshness** axes: matches completed while a web user is offline never reach Convex and nothing backfills them on reconnect; failed quick-match syncs are only recoverable by a manual "Retry" button that disappears when the user leaves the result screen; and the PWA ships `registerType: 'autoUpdate'` + `cleanupOutdatedCaches` with **zero** update-available / reload UX, so a mid-session deploy can orphan lazy-loaded route chunks. No critical (local-data-loss) issue was found.
+
+Severity tally: **0 critical, 3 high, 4 medium, 3 low.**
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] offline-pwa-no-reconnect-backfill — Matches completed offline (web) never sync to cloud and nothing replays them on reconnect
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/auth/bootstrap.js:22-23` — when `isOnline` is false, `getAuthBootstrapMode` returns `{ mode: 'local' }`.
+- `src/auth/AuthContext.jsx:4-14` — `LocalAuthProvider` hard-codes `isAuthenticated: false`, `user: null` for local mode.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:624-628` — `syncCompletedMatch` early-returns and calls `resetSync()` when `!isAuthenticated || !user`.
+- `src/hooks/useMatchSync.js:91-102` — `syncMatch` clears `payloadRef.current = null` when `!isAuthenticated`, so the bootstrap retry effect at `useMatchSync.js:81-89` has nothing to replay.
+- `src/main.jsx:179-202` — the only `online`/`offline` listeners just re-evaluate auth bootstrap; none scan localStorage for unsynced matches.
+
+**What's wrong:** A signed-in user who loses connectivity is dropped into `mode:'local'` where `isAuthenticated=false`. Any match they complete while offline is saved locally but never queued for cloud sync. On reconnect the app flips back to cloud mode and *remounts the tree*, but there is no "find unsynced matches and push them" backfill. The `useMatchSync` bootstrap-retry only replays a payload captured earlier in the same session — which an offline match never produced.
+
+**User impact:** Signed-in web user scores a full match on the train with no signal, gets home, and the match is missing from their cloud profile / cross-device history forever (it stays only on the original device). Affects: signed-in web user offline; signed-in user with flaky connectivity.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Tag locally-saved matches with a `sync.status: 'pending'` marker, and on the `online` event (and on auth-mode flip to cloud) scan localStorage for pending matches and push them via the existing idempotent `clientMatchId` upsert. Convex's `matches.save` already dedups on `clientMatchId` (`convex/matches.ts:92-103`), so replay is safe.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] offline-pwa-no-update-ux — `autoUpdate` + `cleanupOutdatedCaches` with no reload prompt orphans lazy route chunks after a deploy
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `vite.config.js:44-46` — `injectRegister: false`, `registerType: 'autoUpdate'`, `cleanupOutdatedCaches: true`.
+- `src/main.jsx:112-125` — `registerWebServiceWorker` manually calls `navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')` with **no** `updatefound`/`controllerchange` handling and **no** `virtual:pwa-register` import (confirmed: no `virtual:pwa-register`, `registerSW`, `onNeedRefresh`, `controllerchange`, or `skipWaiting` reference anywhere in `src/`).
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:18`, `:1201-1202` — routes are `React.lazy()`-loaded and wrapped in a route-level `ErrorBoundary`.
+
+**What's wrong:** `registerType:'autoUpdate'` generates a service worker that `skipWaiting()` + `clientsClaim()` and (with `cleanupOutdatedCaches`) deletes the previous precache as soon as the new SW activates. The currently-open tab keeps running the old JS, which still references old content-hashed chunk filenames. When the user navigates to a not-yet-loaded lazy route, the old chunk has been purged from cache and is gone from the server (Vercel immutable hashed assets) → the dynamic `import()` rejects → the route `ErrorBoundary` shows "App route crashed." There is no `onNeedRefresh` toast or "Update available — reload" affordance to recover gracefully.
+
+**User impact:** Any user with the tab/PWA open across a production deploy can hit a broken route ("route crashed") until they manually hard-reload. Most likely for engaged users mid-session and installed-PWA users who rarely cold-start. Affects: web + installed PWA across deploys.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Either switch to `registerType:'prompt'` and wire `virtual:pwa-register`'s `onNeedRefresh` to a non-blocking "Update available" banner that calls `updateServiceWorker(true)`, or keep `autoUpdate` but add a `navigator.serviceWorker.addEventListener('controllerchange', () => location.reload())` guard. Today neither exists.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] offline-pwa-quick-sync-retry-fragile — Failed quick-match sync only retriable via a button that vanishes when leaving the result screen
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/hooks/useMatchSync.js:57-65` — sync failure sets `syncState='failed'`; no automatic retry is scheduled.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2677-2685` — the only retry path is a manual "Retry" button rendered solely inside the `phase === 'result'` sync banner.
+- `src/main.jsx:179-202` / `src/components/OfflineFallback.jsx:41-55` — `online` listeners never call `retrySync`.
+
+**What's wrong:** When a signed-in user is online but Convex/Clerk is momentarily unreachable (or they go offline *after* the match started in cloud mode), the quick-match sync fails and surfaces a red banner with a "Retry" button. There is no auto-retry on reconnect, and the retry control only exists on the result screen — navigate away (to history, dashboard, another match) and the failed match can no longer be re-synced from the UI; it also isn't picked up by any background reconnect logic.
+
+**User impact:** Signed-in user finishes a match during a transient outage, doesn't notice/ignores the banner, taps "Back," and the match is now permanently local-only with no path to push it to the cloud. Affects: signed-in web user with flaky network.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Same pending-queue + `online`-event backfill as offline-pwa-no-reconnect-backfill; at minimum, listen for `online` and auto-fire `retrySync` while the result screen is mounted.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] offline-pwa-tournament-sync-fire-forget — Tournament cloud sync is fire-and-forget with a swallowed error and no failed-state
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:60-69` (`saveMatchMutation(payload).catch(() => {})`), and the identical pattern in `MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:71-78`, `MonoCricketLiveScore.jsx:75-82`, `MonoCricketTestLiveScore.jsx:63-70`, `MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:273-280`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Unlike quick matches (which track `syncState` and show a banner), completed *tournament* matches are pushed to Convex fire-and-forget with `.catch(() => {})`. If the mutation rejects (transient network error while nominally "online", server error, WS still reconnecting), the failure is silently swallowed — no `failed` state, no banner, no retry, no pending marker. (Offline tournament matches don't even reach this line because `isAuthenticated` is false in local mode and the function early-returns at e.g. `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:56` — that gap is covered by offline-pwa-no-reconnect-backfill.)
+
+**User impact:** A tournament match that fails to sync during a brief online hiccup diverges silently from the cloud; the local tournament looks complete but the cloud profile/cross-device view is missing that result, with zero indication to the user. Affects: signed-in user running a tournament on flaky network.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Route tournament sync through the same pending/retry machinery as quick matches, or at least record a per-match `sync:'failed'` marker that the reconnect backfill can act on.
+
+**Confidence:** high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] offline-pwa-stale-on-resync — Re-syncing an edited match is a no-op; cloud copy stays stale
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `convex/matches.ts:92-103` — when a match with the same `clientMatchId` already exists, `save` returns `existingMatch._id` early and never patches the row.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:244`, `:352` — `saveTournamentToConvex` is also called from post-completion / correction paths, reusing the same `clientMatchId` (`tournament:<sport>:<tid>:<mid>`, `src/utils/tournamentSync.js:122-124`).
+
+**What's wrong:** The server-side dedup is insert-once: the first sync for a given `clientMatchId` wins and all later syncs are silently ignored. If a match is corrected after its first successful sync (e.g. a goals match finished, then a score correction re-syncs), the cloud retains the original, now-wrong, result.
+
+**User impact:** Edited/corrected match results don't propagate to the cloud; the device and the profile disagree, and the device looks authoritative locally while the cloud is stale. Affects: signed-in user who corrects a result after it first synced.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Make `save` upsert (patch on `clientMatchId` match) instead of returning early, or send a monotonically increasing revision so the server can decide to overwrite.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] offline-pwa-fallback-only-onLine — Offline banner relies solely on `navigator.onLine`; misses captive-portal / no-internet states (web)
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/components/OfflineFallback.jsx:29`, `:43`, `:57` — visibility is driven entirely by `globalThis.navigator.onLine`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:234-252` — an actual reachability probe (`fetch(CONVEX_URL)`) exists, but only `shouldProbeNativeCloud` (native) gates it; web never reachability-probes.
+
+**What's wrong:** `navigator.onLine === true` only means "a network interface is up," not "the internet is reachable." On a captive portal or connected-but-no-internet Wi-Fi, the offline banner never appears, yet cloud auth/sync silently fails. Web users get no signal that they're effectively offline; the 2.5s Convex probe that would catch this is native-only.
+
+**User impact:** Web user on hotel/airport Wi-Fi sees a normal UI, signs-in attempts hang/fail, syncs fail, and nothing explains why. Affects: web user behind captive portal / dead connection.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Add a lightweight reachability heartbeat (reuse the existing `fetch(CONVEX_URL, {mode:'no-cors'})` probe) for web to drive offline state, rather than trusting `navigator.onLine` alone.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] offline-pwa-snapshot-not-reactive — Offline banner's saved-counts snapshot is stale because it only refreshes on online/offline transitions
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/components/OfflineFallback.jsx:30`, `:41-55` — `snapshot` is read once at mount and re-read only on `online`/`offline` events.
+
+**What's wrong:** While the user stays offline and saves several matches/tournaments, the "Saved on this device: N quick matches and M tournaments / Latest quick match: …" line never updates (no storage-change subscription, no per-render read), so it under-reports what was just saved during the offline session.
+
+**User impact:** Minor confusion — the offline banner claims fewer saved matches than actually exist on the device during an extended offline session. Affects: any offline user saving multiple matches in one offline stretch. Non-blocking.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Re-read the snapshot on a `storage` event or when the route changes, or recompute it per render (the read is cheap).
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] offline-pwa-memory-fallback-no-clear — Private-mode memory fallback lacks a `clear()`, breaking tests/callers that call `localStorage.clear()`
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/utils/storage.js:37-50` — `createMemoryFallback` implements `getItem`/`setItem`/`removeItem` but **not** `clear` (or `key`/`length`).
+- `src/utils/storage.js:101-112` — `getStorageUsage` reads `globalThis.localStorage.length/.key`, which don't exist on the memory fallback, so usage always reports 0 in private mode.
+
+**What's wrong:** In Safari Private Mode (where `isStorageAvailable()` is false and the memory fallback is used), any caller relying on `clear()`, `length`, or `key()` against the active backend gets undefined behaviour, and quota/usage warnings are effectively disabled.
+
+**User impact:** Safari private-browsing users get no storage-near-full warnings; cross-session "clear all data" flows that assume `clear()` exists could throw. Niche. Affects: Safari Private Mode users.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Add `clear`, `length`, and `key` to the memory fallback so it is a drop-in `Storage` shim.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] offline-pwa-svg-primary-icons — Manifest's primary 192/512 icons are SVG-only; some installed-PWA surfaces (notably iOS) won't render them
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `vite.config.js:62-72` — the primary `icons[]` entries are `image/svg+xml`; PNG variants exist only with `purpose: 'any maskable'` (`:73-84`).
+
+**What's wrong:** iOS Safari (and a few launchers) ignore SVG manifest icons for the home-screen/installed icon and fall back to a screenshot/letter. The maskable PNGs partially cover this, so it's not a guaranteed blank icon, but the non-maskable primary icon is SVG-only.
+
+**User impact:** Installed PWA may show a generic/low-quality icon on iOS. Cosmetic. Affects: iOS home-screen install.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Provide non-maskable PNG 192/512 entries alongside the SVGs.
+
+**Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] offline-pwa-start-url-landing — `start_url: '/'` opens the installed PWA on the marketing/landing route rather than the app
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `vite.config.js:60` — `start_url: '/'`; `src/designs/design1-mono/index.jsx:1205` — `/` renders `MonoLanding` (guest marketing vs dashboard split).
+
+**What's wrong:** For a signed-out installed-PWA user, launching the app lands on the guest marketing page rather than `/play` or a dashboard, adding a tap before scoring. The `shortcuts` do expose `/play`, but the default launch target is the landing.
+
+**User impact:** Minor extra navigation for installed-PWA users on cold launch. Cosmetic/UX. Affects: installed PWA.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Consider `start_url: '/play'` (or a dashboard route) for the installed experience, since marketing copy is less relevant once installed.
+
+**Confidence:** low.
+
+---
+
+## Non-findings verified (not reported as bugs)
+
+- **`navigateFallback: '/index.html'` with no denylist** (`vite.config.js:112`): not a bug. `navigateFallback` only intercepts same-origin *navigation* requests; Convex (WSS, `*.convex.cloud`) and Clerk are cross-origin XHR/WS and are additionally `NetworkOnly` (`vite.config.js:113-126`), so they are never served the SPA shell.
+- **Duplicate matches on reconnect:** mitigated. `convex/matches.ts:92-103` dedups on `clientMatchId`, so replaying a sync cannot create duplicates (the inverse stale-on-resync issue is captured separately above).
