+# Tournament system
+
+## Summary
+
+I traced the full tournament lifecycle — setup wizard, round-robin/bracket generation, standings/NRR math, knockout phase transition, match scoring + completion, persistence/resume, and edit/delete safety — across `MonoTournamentSetup`, `MonoTournamentList`, the three engine tournaments (`GenericSetsTournament`, `GenericGoalsTournament`, `MonoCricketTournament`), `KnockoutMatchCard`, `MonoTournamentLiveScore`, and the calc utils (`roundRobin`, `knockoutManager`, `standingsCalculator`, `cricketCalculations`, `tournamentDisplay`, `tournamentSync`). Bracket generation (circle method) and the unit-tested standings/NRR math are sound. The most serious issue is in the goals scorer's timed auto-finish path, which can complete a no-draw match as a `'draw'` and corrupt both standings and the knockout bracket. Most other findings are integration gaps (stale bracket after group edit, cricket knockout score not rendered) and edge-case UX/data-loss windows.
+
+Severity tally: Critical 1 · High 3 · Medium 5 · Low 5
+
+---
+
+### [CRITICAL] Timed goals match that expires tied is saved as `winner: 'draw'` even in no-draw sports — breaks standings and knockout bracket
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:142-153` (timed auto-finish) calls `winner: determineWinner(score1, score2, m)`; `determineWinner` (`:17-21`) returns `'draw'` when `s1 === s2`. The manual `saveMatch` path guards this (`:325-328` blocks save when `!drawAllowed && score1 === score2`) but the **timed auto-end path has no such guard**. Basketball (`src/models/sportRegistry.js:222 drawAllowed: false`) and at least one other goals sport (`:429 drawAllowed: false`) both expose `timePresets`, so a timed match auto-ends at the limit regardless of score.
+
+**What's wrong:** When the clock expires on a tied no-draw match, the match is auto-committed with `status: 'completed'`, `winner: 'draw'`. Two downstream failures result:
+1. **Standings (phantom game):** `calculateGoalsStandings` (`src/utils/standingsCalculator.js:139-148`) only records a draw's points/W-D-L when `drawAllowed` is true. With `drawAllowed:false` the match increments `played` and goals for/against but awards no points and no W/D/L — a silently uncounted "completed" game. (`standingsCalculator.test.js:270-281` confirms this is the produced state.)
+2. **Knockout (broken bracket):** if the tied match is a semi-final, `updateKnockoutBracket` (`src/utils/knockoutManager.js:65-68`) computes `semiWinner = semi.winner` = `'draw'` and `semiLoser = semi.winner === semi.team1Id ? semi.team2Id : semi.team1Id` = `team1Id`. The final is then seeded `team1Id: 'draw'`, and `getTeamName('draw')` renders **"Unknown"**. A timed-format playoff that ends level produces an unresolvable/garbage final.
+
+**User impact:** Basketball is the headline case — a no-draw sport that is naturally timed and frequently ends regulation tied. The user sees the match marked complete, standings that don't add up, and (in playoffs) a final between "Unknown" and a real team that can never be correctly decided.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Apply the same draw guard used in `saveMatch` to the timed auto-finish (and ideally force an overtime/shootout resolution prompt) before writing `winner`. Never persist `winner: 'draw'` when `sportConfig.config.drawAllowed === false`.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Editing or clearing a group match after the knockout stage starts leaves the bracket seeded from stale standings
+
+**Evidence:** `src/utils/knockoutManager.js:18-29` (`initializeKnockoutStage`) early-returns once `knockoutMatches.length > 0`; the phase-transition effects in all three tournaments (`GenericSetsTournament.jsx:70-85`, `GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:46-61`, `MonoCricketTournament.jsx:187-202`) likewise bail when KO matches already exist. `updateKnockoutBracket` (`knockoutManager.js:36-85`) only re-seeds final/3rd-place from completed semis — it never re-reads group standings. The "Clear" control renders on every completed group match in the Matches tab (`GenericSetsTournament.jsx:271-279`, `GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:229-237`, `MonoCricketTournament.jsx:420-430`) regardless of `tournament.phase`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Once the group completes and the bracket is generated from standings, a user can still clear/re-enter a group result. Standings recompute (they are derived via `useMemo`), but the already-generated knockout `team1Id/team2Id` seeds are frozen. The bracket no longer reflects who actually finished 1st–4th.
+
+**User impact:** The wrong teams play the semis/final after a late group-score correction, with no warning. Silent correctness bug in the core group-to-playoff flow.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Either disable group-match Clear/edit once `phase === 'knockout'`, or re-derive and re-seed the (still-pending) knockout matches when group results change. At minimum warn the user that the bracket is locked.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Cricket knockout matches never display a score in `KnockoutMatchCard`
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/KnockoutMatchCard.jsx:18-20` sets `hasScore` for `engine === 'custom-cricket'`, but the score-render blocks only exist for `engine === 'sets'` (`:72-81, :104-126`) and `engine === 'goals'` (`:77-99`). There is no cricket branch. `MonoCricketTournament.jsx:457-468 / 595-648` render all knockout matches (semis/final/3rd) through this card with `engine="custom-cricket"`.
+
+**What's wrong:** A completed cricket semi-final/final shows team names + a "Completed" badge + "Edit Score" button but no runs/wickets/result. The winner is also not visually distinguished in the card body (the winner star/coloring used in the group `renderLimitedComplete` path is absent here).
+
+**User impact:** Cricket tournament knockout results are invisible on the card — the user must open the scorer to see what happened. Inconsistent with the rich group-match cards in the same screen.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Add a `custom-cricket` score block to `KnockoutMatchCard` (runs/wickets + winDesc), mirroring `renderLimitedComplete`/`renderTestComplete` in `MonoCricketTournament.jsx`.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Cricket points-table tie-break is points→NRR only; ties in points+NRR seed the bracket non-deterministically and ignore wins/head-to-head
+
+**Evidence:** `src/utils/cricketCalculations.js:348-351` sorts only by `points` then `nrr`. The sorted table is passed straight into `generateKnockoutMatches` as standings (`MonoCricketTournament.jsx:193`), which seeds 1v4 / 2v3 by array index (`roundRobin.js:80-99`).
+
+**What's wrong:** Real cricket tables break ties by wins, then head-to-head, then NRR. Here, two teams level on points and NRR (common with few matches / identical scorelines) fall back to `Array.prototype.sort` order, which is not guaranteed stable across engines for the original insertion order and carries no sporting tiebreak. That order then determines seeding (who is "1st" vs "2nd"), which changes the bracket and, in a `winnerMode: 'table-topper'` cricket tournament, determines the champion outright.
+
+**User impact:** The displayed standings order — and therefore the tournament winner / bracket seeding — can be arbitrary when teams are level. Users will perceive a wrong result.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Extend the comparator with explicit tiebreakers (wins, then a head-to-head pass, then NRR, then a stable fallback such as team name) so ranking is deterministic and defensible.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Undo-delete restores a full snapshot, silently discarding tournaments created/edited after the delete
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoTournamentList.jsx:65-82`. `deleteTournament` captures `snapshot = loadSportTournaments(...)` at delete time; `undoDeleteTournament` writes that whole snapshot back via `saveData(...)` (`:79`).
+
+**What's wrong:** Undo overwrites the entire sport's tournament list with the pre-delete snapshot. Any tournament created or modified between the delete and the undo (for this sport, in the same list view) is lost. The window is narrowed because navigating away and back clears `deletedTournament` (`:53`), but in-view creation/edit is still reachable.
+
+**User impact:** Rare but real data loss on undo.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Undo should re-insert only the deleted tournament (merge by id) rather than replacing the whole list.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] A "completed" cricket match with no innings and no scores inflates `played` with no result
+
+**Evidence:** `src/utils/cricketCalculations.js:317-342`. After incrementing `t1.played++/t2.played++` (`:324-325`), if neither `match.innings` nor `match.team1Score && match.team2Score` is present, the function `return`s (`:337-339`) before `applyMatchResult`, leaving a played game with no W/L/points and no NRR contribution.
+
+**What's wrong:** Any path that marks a cricket match `status: 'completed'` without persisting score shapes (e.g. a partially-cleared match, or a future scorer change) counts toward `played` but contributes nothing else, and NRR denominators stay 0.
+
+**User impact:** Edge-case standings distortion (a team shows extra games played with no points). Low likelihood under normal scoring but unguarded.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Skip `played++` until a valid result shape is confirmed, or treat as "no result" explicitly (a `noResult` field already exists on the row, `:313`, but is never incremented).
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Knockout seeding silently produces permanent `TBD` if standings are shorter than the requested advancing count
+
+**Evidence:** `src/utils/roundRobin.js:65-124`. For `teamsAdvancing === 4`, seeds read `standings[0..3]?.teamId || null` (`:84-98`). If standings has <4 entries, the missing slots are `null`; `KnockoutMatchCard` then renders "TBD" with "Waiting for semi-final results" forever (`KnockoutMatchCard.jsx:139-143`).
+
+**What's wrong:** The setup wizard currently gates this (Top-4 is `disabled` when `teamCount < 4`, `MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:1288`, and team-count changes reset `teamsAdvancing`, `:605-608`), so it is not reachable through the happy-path UI. But the generator itself has no guard, so any imported/migrated/edited tournament with a mismatched `knockoutConfig` produces a dead bracket with no error.
+
+**User impact:** A malformed or migrated tournament shows an unplayable knockout stage with no explanation.
+
+**Suggested direction:** In `generateKnockoutMatches`, clamp `teamsAdvancing` to `standings.length` (fall back to a 2-team final) and surface a warning rather than emitting `null` seeds.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Group-stage completion uses match `status`, but standings/sync use multiple completion heuristics — divergent definitions of "done"
+
+**Evidence:** `isGroupStageComplete` (`src/utils/knockoutManager.js:9-11`) requires every match `status === 'completed'`. But `MonoTournamentList` measures progress via `isTournamentMatchCompleted` (`tournamentSync.js:99-112`), which for sets infers completion from set counts/format even without `status`, and `GenericSetsTournament` runs a repair pass (`GenericSetsTournament.jsx:30-49`) that flips `status` to `completed` on load when sets imply a finished match.
+
+**What's wrong:** A sets tournament whose last match has completed sets but a stale non-`completed` status will show "all complete" in the list (`isTournamentMatchCompleted`) yet NOT trigger the knockout transition (`isGroupStageComplete`) until the repair pass runs on entering the detail screen. The two surfaces disagree about whether the group is finished.
+
+**User impact:** The list says the tournament is fully played, but the knockout tab still says "Knockout stage begins after all group matches are completed" until the user opens and re-saves the tournament. Confusing dead-end.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Make `isGroupStageComplete` use the same `isTournamentMatchCompleted` heuristic as the list/sync layer, or guarantee the repair pass runs before the transition check.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Knockout score-clear in `GenericSetsTournament` bypasses the undo-able score-clear flow used for group matches
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/GenericSetsTournament.jsx:139-147` defines `deleteKnockoutScore` which immediately wipes `sets/status/winner` with no confirm and no undo, whereas group matches use `useTournamentScoreClear` (`:96`, `hooks/useTournamentScoreClear.js`) with a confirm panel and undo. `GenericGoalsTournament` and `MonoCricketTournament` expose no knockout clear at all.
+
+**What's wrong:** Inconsistent and unsafe: clearing a final/semi result has no confirmation or undo, while clearing a group result does. (Note: `deleteKnockoutScore` also appears to have no caller wired into the rendered KO cards, so the safe-guarded path may simply be missing for knockout matches entirely.)
+
+**User impact:** Either an unguarded destructive action or no way to fix a mis-entered knockout score, depending on which path is reachable.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Route knockout score clears through the same confirm+undo hook, covering all three engines.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Duplicate team names are accepted at creation
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:285` only rejects empty names (`teams.some(t => !t.name.trim())`); no uniqueness check.
+
+**What's wrong:** Two teams can share a name. Standings/scoring key off unique `team.id` so results stay correct, but the schedule, standings, and match cards become ambiguous ("Team A vs Team A").
+
+**User impact:** Cosmetic confusion only.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Warn (don't necessarily block) on duplicate names in step 3/review.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Dead `#0066ff` blue accent throughout the tournament UI contradicts the green design system
+
+**Evidence:** Hardcoded `#0066ff` appears across tournament views, e.g. `MonoCricketTournament.jsx:47,66,124,319,548`, `GenericSetsTournament.jsx:186,223,547`, `GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:152,483`, `MonoTournamentSetup.jsx` (active step, badges, borders), `MonoTournamentList.jsx:232,258`. Project memory states the blue accent is retired in favor of `var(--primary)` field green and "any leftovers should be hunted down."
+
+**What's wrong:** Tournament screens still render the deprecated blue for progress bars, active tabs, badges, NRR stars, and the champion border instead of the green token.
+
+**User impact:** Visual inconsistency with the rest of the app's green Mono identity.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Replace hardcoded `#0066ff` with the `var(--primary)` / `--accent` tokens.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] `getNrrColor` uses hardcoded green/red not aligned with design tokens; NRR sign edge at exactly 0
+
+**Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoCricketTournament.jsx:34-38,553`. Color thresholds are literal hex; the `+`/`-` prefix logic at `:553` (`row.nrr > 0 ? '+' : ''`) shows no sign for exactly 0 (fine) but `-0.000` can appear from `toFixed(3)` of a tiny negative NRR.
+
+**What's wrong:** Minor: a near-zero negative NRR can render as `-0.000`.
+
+**User impact:** Trivial cosmetic.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Normalize `-0` and route colors through tokens.
+
+**Confidence:** medium
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Series tournament label/progress assumes exactly 2 teams; `teamCount` not pinned for series
+
+**Evidence:** `MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:570-574` sets `teamCount = 2` for series, and `generateMatches` (`:261-268`) always uses `teams[0]/teams[1]`. `MonoTournamentList.jsx:240` keys the "series" label off `t.teams?.length === 2`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Robust today, but if a series is ever created/imported with !=2 teams, only the first two are scheduled and the list label silently falls through to the round-robin branch.
+
+**User impact:** None on the happy path; latent fragility for imported data.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Assert/clamp series to exactly 2 teams at creation and in the label logic.
+
+**Confidence:** low
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] `updateMatchInTournament` matches by `id` OR `Number(id)`, risking the wrong match when string/number ids collide
+
+**Evidence:** `src/utils/knockoutManager.js:132-172` and `findMatchInTournament` match `m.id === matchId || m.id === Number(matchId)`. Group match ids are template strings like `"${Date.now()}-0"` (`MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:263,270`) while `Number("...-0")` is `NaN`, so collisions are unlikely — but cricket tournament lookups also do `t.id === Number(id) || t.id === id` (`MonoCricketTournament.jsx:168`) where tournament `id` is a numeric `Date.now()`.
+
+**What's wrong:** The loose numeric coercion is defensive but could mis-match if any future id is a bare numeric string shared between a group and knockout match.
+
+**User impact:** None observed; latent.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Normalize id types at creation and compare strictly.
+
+**Confidence:** low
+
+---
+
+## Notes on things checked and found correct
+
+- **Round-robin circle method** (`roundRobin.js:9-57`) is correct: post-BYE even `n`, the fixed team plus `rotating[i]`/`rotating[n-1-i]` pairing consumes every rotating index exactly once per round; BYE matches are excluded; odd team counts handled. Matches the green `roundRobin.test.js`.
+- **Pure-knockout creation** is sound: `MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:305-324` creates `type:'knockout'` with `phase:'knockout'` and pre-seeded `knockoutMatches`, so it does not get stuck on the `isGroupStageComplete` (0/0) transition.
+- **Top-4 / 3rd-place gating** in setup correctly disables/resets for `teamCount < 4` (`:605-608, :1288, :1299`).
+- **Sets/goals standings math** (sets diff, GD, points) matches the passing `standingsCalculator.test.js`.
