+# UX/UI Consistency & Visual Design
+
+## Summary
+
+The "Mono" green-monotone redesign is only half-applied. The marketing surfaces (`GuestLanding`, `MonoSportHome`) correctly consume the green `sportsTokens`/`landingTokenBridge` system, but the **entire functional app** — the signed-in dashboard, the QuickMatch setup, every live-scoring engine (sets/goals/cricket/tennis), history, statistics, and tournaments — still hardcodes the dead `#0066ff` blue (106 occurrences across 19 production files), plus orange/green accents and a `1.5px` border weight the design system explicitly bans. The two homepages a user sees (`/` guest vs `/` signed-in) look like two different products. The bridge that was built to fix this (`sportsCssVariables`, `landingTokenBridge`) is wired into tests but never applied to the DOM, so even the global app chrome renders at `1.5px`. No true criticals were found (the one broken-link candidate, `/game/:id`, is dormant because its session writer is unrouted); the dominant issues are high-severity visual-consistency regressions.
+
+**Severity tally:** Critical 0 · High 4 · Medium 6 · Low 5
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Signed-in dashboard renders on the dead `#0066ff` blue token set, not the green monotone
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/landing/DashboardLanding.jsx:15-49` defines a local token object `t = { blue: '#0066ff', green: '#16a34a', orange: '#ea580c', border: '#e8e8e8' ... }` and uses it for every accent (progress bar `:469`, step heads `:411`, mode cards, sport tiles `:664`, active-session card `:33`, all primary buttons `:39-43`). A ready-made green replacement exists and is ignored: `src/designs/design1-mono/theme/sportsTokens.js:235-258` exports `landingTokenBridge` (`blue: action(green)`, `borderWeight: '1px'`), which `GuestLanding` already consumes via `landingTheme.js`.
+- **What's wrong:** `DashboardLanding` is the signed-in homepage (the `SignedIn` branch of `MonoLanding`). It was never migrated off the pre-redesign blue. MEMORY.md is explicit: "Old `#0066ff` blue is dead — hunt down any leftovers."
+- **User impact:** A signed-in user who saves a match (`saveQuickMatch` → `se_quickmatches`, confirmed same key the dashboard reads at `:12`) lands on a blue/orange dashboard that clashes with the green guest landing, the green `/play` picker, and the green app chrome. Brand feels broken/unfinished.
+- **Suggested direction:** Replace the local `t`/`s` token objects with `landingTokenBridge` (or `sportsTokens`); delete the blue/orange literals.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [HIGH] Live scoring + QuickMatch setup hardcode the dead blue as the primary accent (team 1 = blue)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2354-2355` — `const leftAccent = leftTeam === 1 ? '#0066ff' : '#16a34a'` (team 1 brandcolor IS the dead blue in the inline goals/sets scoreboard). Setup step dots `:1410` `background: i < setupStep ? '#0066ff' : '#eee'`; format-change link `:1520`; sync banner `:2667-2668`. `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:558,590` SERVE indicator `color: '#0066ff'`; side-swap highlight `:498-499`; undo button `:656`. Total: 106 `#0066ff` hits across 19 non-showcase files (`MonoQuickMatch`, all 5 `scoring/*`, `MonoHistory`, `MonoStatistics`, `MonoTournamentList/Setup`, `MonoCricketTournament`, `Generic*Tournament`, `MonoOnboarding`, `PlayerSearchInput`).
+- **What's wrong:** The actual product (where users spend their time) is still on the retired blue palette; the green redesign stopped at the landing layer.
+- **User impact:** The most-used surface — keeping score live — shows team 1 in dead blue against a green-branded shell. Affects every sport, every context (web/mobile/Android).
+- **Suggested direction:** Sweep `#0066ff` → `var(--se-color-action)` / `getSportAccent()`; for team-vs-team accents use two distinct token-derived colors instead of blue/green literals.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [HIGH] `--se-border-standard` renders at 1.5px app-wide, violating the "no 1.5px anywhere" rule; the 1px override is dead
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/index.css:74` `--se-border-standard: 1.5px` is the ONLY definition in any `.css` (verified). `sportsTokens.js:227` would override it to `1px` via `sportsCssVariables`, but `sportsCssVariables` is referenced **only in `theme/sportsTokens.test.js`** — never applied to a DOM node. So `var(--se-border-standard)` resolves to 1.5px in the global nav (`index.jsx:555`), confirm dialog (`:633,675`), scoring notice (`:705`), bottom nav (`:937`), and the AppLoading board (`index.css:224`).
+- **What's wrong:** Design system mandates 1px edges / 2px emphasis with "no 1.5px anywhere (exception: dark scorecard internal 1.5px)." The app chrome breaks this on every screen, and the intended fix is unreachable code.
+- **User impact:** Subtly-off line weights throughout the persistent navigation and dialogs; inconsistent with the 1px hairlines used elsewhere.
+- **Suggested direction:** Change `index.css:74` to `1px`, or actually inject `sportsCssVariables` at the app root. Then audit remaining literal `1.5px` (16 inline occurrences in `DashboardLanding`, `GuestLanding`, `MonoQuickMatch`, `MonoHistory`, `MonoStatistics`).
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [HIGH] QuickMatch result screen has no winner emphasis and a flat 6-button action wall
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2700-2701` winner headline `style={{ color: '#111' }}` — identical ink to every other label; no accent, no celebration. Actions `:2796-2817` render six buttons where only "Rematch" is `mono-btn-primary` and the other five (Share, View History, See Stats, New Match, Home) are visually identical `mono-btn` with no grouping. The celebration CSS (`mono-confetti`, `mono-set-won`, `mono-match-complete`) IS used in `MonoSetsLiveScore`/`MonoTennisLiveScore` but not on this end-of-match result screen.
+- **What's wrong:** The payoff moment of the core flow is undersold (winner indistinguishable from body text) while presenting six equal-weight choices with no hierarchy. "New Match" vs "Home" vs "View History" compete.
+- **User impact:** Anticlimactic result; users must read all six button labels to find the one they want.
+- **Suggested direction:** Accent the winner (token green / sport accent); group actions (1 primary "Rematch", a secondary pair, a tertiary text row for Home/Stats); consider reusing the existing set-won celebration.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Active-session card links to a non-existent `/game/:id` route (latent dead-end)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/landing/DashboardLanding.jsx:576` `onClick={() => navigate('/game/${session.id}')}`. No `path="game/:id"` exists in the router (`index.jsx:1205-1246`); it would hit `NotFoundRoute` ("This screen is not available"). Currently dormant: the card only renders when `getActiveSessions()` returns rows (`universalStorage.js:47`), but `gs_sessions` is written only by `useGameSession`, used solely by `MonoSetup`/`MonoLiveGame`, which are **not routed**. The live flow (`MonoQuickMatch`) never writes `gs_sessions`.
+- **What's wrong:** A prominent "Resume →" CTA points at a 404. Inert today, but any future code path that writes an active session resurrects a broken core flow.
+- **User impact:** None for current users; high-risk regression if session persistence is re-enabled.
+- **Suggested direction:** Point the card at the real scoring route, or remove the dead active-session branch.
+- **Confidence:** high (that the route is missing); medium (on user reachability)
+
+### [MEDIUM] Two homepage layouts diverge structurally, not just in color
+
+- **Evidence:** `GuestLanding.jsx` is a full marketing page (hero ticker, 14-sport grid, features, 3 steps, CTA, footer with Privacy/Terms/Contact). `DashboardLanding.jsx:556-752` (`ExistingUserDashboard`) is a 672px app column with a different sticky nav (`:878`), different nav items (History/Statistics/Find players/@username), and a minimal footer. The guest footer exposes legal links + `© 2026`; the dashboard footer has none and reads `© 2025`.
+- **What's wrong:** Beyond palette, the chrome (nav, max-width, footer) is inconsistent between the two `/` states.
+- **User impact:** Signing in changes the whole spatial language of "home," not just content.
+- **Suggested direction:** Unify nav/footer chrome; both should share the global nav or a consistent variant.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [MEDIUM] Stale / inconsistent copyright year (`© 2025` vs `© 2026`)
+
+- **Evidence:** `DashboardLanding.jsx:943` `&copy; 2025`; `GuestLanding.jsx:745` `&copy; 2026`. Current date is 2026-06-22.
+- **What's wrong:** Hardcoded, divergent, and one is already stale.
+- **User impact:** Looks unmaintained; differs depending on auth state.
+- **Suggested direction:** Single shared footer component with `new Date().getFullYear()`.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [MEDIUM] Functional screens bypass design tokens for ink/levels, hardcoding `#111/#888/#666/#bbb/#555`
+
+- **Evidence:** `MonoQuickMatch.jsx` setup + result use literal greys throughout (`:135-140, 1386-1647, 2604-2782`); `ErrorBoundary.jsx:51-58` (`#888/#111/#666`); `index.jsx` NotFound `:59-65` and Tournament-not-found `:981,1000` (`#888`). The token system provides `--se-color-ink / ink-soft / ink-muted / ink-faint` for exactly these.
+- **What's wrong:** Greyscale ramp is duplicated by hand, so it can drift from the tokens and won't respond to any theme change.
+- **User impact:** Low individually, but it's the mechanism by which screens fall out of sync.
+- **Suggested direction:** Replace literal greys with the `--se-color-ink*` tokens.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [MEDIUM] DashboardLanding uses an off-scale radius set (6/8/10/20px) instead of the 0/4/8 scale
+
+- **Evidence:** `DashboardLanding.jsx:23` `r: 6`; sport cards `borderRadius: 8` (`:28`); pill badges `borderRadius: 10` (`:352,387,583,743`) and `20` (`:478,498`); step circles `borderRadius:'50%'`. The system radius scale is 0 (brutal) / 4 (`--radius`) / 8 (`--se-radius-card`).
+- **What's wrong:** 6/10/20px are not on the scale; the rounded pills/cards read softer than the rest of the app's sharp Mono identity.
+- **User impact:** Dashboard feels like a different, rounder design language.
+- **Suggested direction:** Snap to 0/4/8; use `pill` (999px) only where a true pill is intended.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [MEDIUM] Guest landing's primary navigation is hidden (`display:none` + `aria-hidden`), so there's no in-page sign-in/section nav
+
+- **Evidence:** `GuestLanding.jsx:231` `<nav aria-hidden="true" style={{ display: 'none' }}>` wraps the brand, the Features/Experience/Sports/How anchors, and the Sign-in button — all permanently hidden. The only persistent nav is the global app header from `index.jsx`.
+- **What's wrong:** Dead nav markup; the section anchors (`#features`, etc.) and the landing-level "Sign in" affordance never render. A guest relies entirely on the global header / hero buttons.
+- **User impact:** Minor for guests (global nav still present), but it's confusing dead code and removes the intended in-page section jumps.
+- **Suggested direction:** Delete the hidden nav, or restore it if the section anchors are meant to be reachable.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] GuestLanding sport cards hardcode `1.5px` borders despite the page otherwise using the 1px `borderWeight` token
+
+- **Evidence:** `GuestLanding.jsx:615` `border: '1.5px ${...} ${...}'` on each sport tile, while the rest of the page uses `t.borderWeight` (= `1px`). Same `1.5px` literal hides in `DashboardLanding.jsx:33,47,218,243,262,346,381,615`.
+- **User impact:** Sport tiles are subtly heavier than surrounding hairlines.
+- **Suggested direction:** Use `t.borderWeight`.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [LOW] Hero ticker is hidden on mobile, dropping social-proof content
+
+- **Evidence:** `GuestLanding.jsx:429` ticker `display: mobile ? 'none' : 'block'`. The `tickerItems` content (and its rAF animation, `:76-91`) never shows on phones — the primary target platform per the hero copy ("Built for web, Android, and iOS").
+- **User impact:** Mobile guests miss the marquee content; minor.
+- **Suggested direction:** Show a static or reduced ticker on mobile, or remove the unused mobile code paths.
+- **Confidence:** medium
+
+### [LOW] Celebration animations hardcode non-token greens
+
+- **Evidence:** `mono.css:818-819` `match-complete` keyframe `background:#e8f5e9 / #c8e6c9`; `:866` `mono-set-won` `background: rgba(47,125,50,0.95)`. These are not the token field-green (`--se-color-action`).
+- **User impact:** Celebration green differs slightly from brand green; only visible mid-animation.
+- **Suggested direction:** Use `color-mix` over `--se-color-action`.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [LOW] `secondaryPriorityActionStyle` and a divider hardcode `#fff` / `#ddd` in the otherwise-tokenized MonoSportHome
+
+- **Evidence:** `MonoSportHome.jsx:178` `background: '#fff'`; `:313` `<span style={{ color: '#ddd' }}>|</span>`. Everything else in this file uses `sportsTokens`.
+- **User impact:** Negligible; consistency nit.
+- **Suggested direction:** `sportsTokens.color.surface` and `sportsTokens.color.line`.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [LOW] Result screen and ErrorBoundary repeat the same flat multi-secondary-button pattern
+
+- **Evidence:** `ErrorBoundary.jsx:75-108` (1 primary + 3 identical secondaries), mirroring the result-screen wall. `NotFoundRoute` (`index.jsx:68-85`) handles this better (Play primary / Home secondary).
+- **User impact:** Minor; choice overload on fallback screens.
+- **Suggested direction:** Reduce to a primary + one or two secondaries; demote the rest to text links.
+- **Confidence:** medium
