+# Sets Scoring Engine Audit (volleyball, badminton, table-tennis, tennis, pickleball, squash)
+
+## Summary
+
+The sets engine is split across **two independent scorers** that do not share completion logic: the quick-match inline scorer in `MonoQuickMatch.jsx` (best-of via `utils/quickMatchSets.js`, single-set via `utils/volleyballCalculations.validateSingleSetScore`) and the tournament scorer `scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx` (its own private `checkSetComplete`). The two implementations disagree at boundary scores, and the single-set path does not enforce win-by-2 at all. Tennis quick-match diverts to a dedicated scorer, but the other five sets sports run through these shared paths. The strongest defects are: a single-set game that ends on a 1-point margin (e.g. 25-24) despite the on-screen "win by 2" rule (CRITICAL), and a badminton best-of game in the tournament scorer that can never complete at the 30-point cap (CRITICAL). Per-sport point targets configured in `setFormats[].points` are effectively dead — every setup UI hardcodes 10/15/21/25 — so badminton/table-tennis/tennis offer wrong point options (HIGH). The existing green unit suite covers `quickMatchSets` and `validateSetScore` but does NOT cover `MonoSetsLiveScore.checkSetComplete`, and one test actively encodes the win-by-2 single-set bug as expected behavior.
+
+Severity tally: **2 critical, 3 high, 4 medium, 3 low**.
+
+---
+
+### [CRITICAL] Single-set games end on a 1-point margin — win-by-2 not enforced
+
+`src/utils/volleyballCalculations.js:13-21` (`validateSingleSetScore`), consumed by `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1034` and `:1139`.
+
+What's wrong: `validateSingleSetScore` returns `true` for any score where the winner has reached `target` and the scores are not tied, EXCEPT the narrow case where the loser is also `>= target` and the winner is below `target + 1`. It never requires a 2-point margin at the first deuce point. Verified empirically: `validateSingleSetScore(25,24,25) === true`, `validateSingleSetScore(11,10,11) === true`, `validateSingleSetScore(15,14,15) === true`. The deuce guard at line 19 only catches loser-also-at-target situations (e.g. 10-10 at target 10), not winner-at-target / loser-at-target-1.
+
+In quick-match single-set mode (`addPoint`, line 1034), the match auto-finalizes the instant this returns true, so a volleyball/badminton/table-tennis/pickleball/squash single set to 25 ends at **25-24** (and to 11 ends at 11-10). `finalizeMatch` (line 642) immediately switches to the result phase and persists, so there is no in-flow undo — the wrong result is recorded.
+
+User impact: A single-set game is declared won and saved on a 1-point lead, directly contradicting the "Win by 2 at deuce" text shown on the same screen (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2628-2630`). Wrong, user-visible, unrecoverable result.
+
+Suggested direction: Enforce `max - min >= winBy` (with `winBy` from sport config, default 2) in `validateSingleSetScore`, mirroring `quickMatchSets.isSetComplete`. Update `volleyballCalculations.test.js:90` which currently asserts `validateSingleSetScore(11,10) === true` as "deuce resolution" — that assertion locks in the bug.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [CRITICAL] Badminton best-of game cannot complete at the 30-point cap in the tournament scorer
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:128-162` (`checkSetComplete`), best-of branch lines 148-161.
+
+What's wrong: the win-by check runs BEFORE the cap check. Order is: `if (max - min < winBy) return false;` (line 156) then `if (maxPoints && max >= maxPoints && max > min) return true;` (line 159). At 30-29 the win-by guard fires first (`30-29 < 2`) and returns false, so the cap (`maxPoints: 30` for badminton) is never reached. Verified empirically: tournament logic returns `false` for 30-29, whereas the quick-match util `quickMatchSets.isSetComplete` (which checks the cap FIRST, `quickMatchSets.js:41`) returns `true`. From 29-29 the game can only reach 30-29 (false) → 30-30 → 31-30 (diff 1, false) → ... it never terminates.
+
+User impact: In a badminton **tournament** match (this scorer is the tournament path), a game that reaches deuce in the cap region (29-29) can never be completed — the scorer is stuck. The same sport scored via quick-match completes correctly because it uses the other util. The two engines disagree on a real BWF boundary.
+
+Suggested direction: Reorder so the cap check precedes the win-by check (as `quickMatchSets.isSetComplete` already does), or have both scorers call the single shared util. No test currently exercises `MonoSetsLiveScore.checkSetComplete`.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Per-sport set-point options are dead config — every setup UI hardcodes 10/15/21/25
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1843` and `:1864` (uses `POINTS_PRESETS`), `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:1199` and `:1411` (hardcoded `[10,15,21,25]`). Source of the ignored data: `src/models/sportRegistry.js` `setFormats[].points` arrays (badminton `[11,15,21]` line 49, table-tennis `[7,11,21]` line 76, tennis `[4,6]` line 106, pickleball `[9,11,15]` line 135, volleyball `[10,15,21,25]` line 18).
+
+What's wrong: Both the quick-match "Points per set" / "Points to win" pickers and the tournament point pickers render a single hardcoded 10/15/21/25 list (`POINTS_PRESETS` from `volleyballCalculations.js:91`). The per-sport `points` arrays in `setFormats` are never read for the picker. So badminton cannot be set to 11, table-tennis cannot be set to 7, and tennis (single-set in tournament) is offered 10/15/21/25 "games" instead of 4/6.
+
+User impact: Users of non-volleyball sets sports get wrong/irrelevant point targets and cannot pick the sport-correct value from the UI; the carefully-authored per-sport options are unreachable.
+
+Suggested direction: Drive the point-preset buttons from the selected `setFormats` entry's `points` array (falling back to `POINTS_PRESETS`), in all four pickers.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Quick-match never offers side-out scoring for volleyball/pickleball despite registry config
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:545` (`tracksPointWinnerServe = sport === 'volleyball' || sport === 'badminton'`), `:1005`, `:1101`; registry `sportRegistry.js:23,139` advertise `scoringModes: ['rally','side-out']`.
+
+What's wrong: The quick-match inline scorer has no scoring-mode toggle and no side-out logic. `tracksPointWinnerServe` simply sets `servingTeam = team` on every point (winner serves) — pure rally behavior — and there is no `scoringMode` state in this path. The side-out implementation (a non-serving tap switches serve without a point) exists only in the tournament scorer `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:219-223`. So volleyball/pickleball quick matches are always rally, even though the sport config (and the sport's real traditional rules for volleyball side-out) lists side-out as a supported mode.
+
+User impact: A user expecting side-out (traditional volleyball) scoring in a quick match cannot get it; only rally is possible. Registry capability is silently unavailable in the most-used flow.
+
+Suggested direction: Either surface the scoring-mode toggle in quick-match (reuse the tournament side-out logic) or document that quick-match is rally-only and remove the implied capability.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Standard-mode point cap (volleyball 27) is silently ignored by the tournament scorer
+
+`src/utils/sportDefaults.js:11-14` (volleyball `customization.pointCap: 27`), `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:131` (`const { winBy, maxPoints } = sportConfig.config;`).
+
+What's wrong: `applyStandardDefaults` injects `customization.pointCap` into the format (volleyball 27, badminton 30 — `sportDefaults.js:11,23`). The tournament scorer reads the cap only from `sportConfig.config.maxPoints`, never from `format.customization.pointCap`. Volleyball's registry config has NO `maxPoints` (`sportRegistry.js:13-26`), so the standard 27-cap never applies in tournament play; the set runs unbounded (29-27, 40-38, ...). Badminton's cap happens to also live in `config.maxPoints: 30`, so it is "wired" — but then breaks per the CRITICAL ordering bug above. The quick-match best-of path DOES honor `format.customization.pointCap` via `getSetWinRule` (`quickMatchSets.js:31`), so the two engines diverge again.
+
+User impact: Volleyball tournament sets ignore the advertised cap; quick-match volleyball respects it. Inconsistent set-end behavior for the same sport depending on flow.
+
+Suggested direction: In `MonoSetsLiveScore.checkSetComplete`, resolve the cap from `effectiveFormat.customization?.pointCap || sportConfig.config.maxPoints`, matching `getSetWinRule`.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Tournament best-of "Sets" picker includes the single-set option, producing type:'best-of' + sets:1
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:1180` (maps `setFormats` without filtering `f.sets > 1`).
+
+What's wrong: In best-of mode, the Sets buttons iterate the full `setFormats`, including the entry with `sets: 1` ("Single set"/"Single game"). Clicking it sets `sets: 1` while `type` remains `'best-of'`. Downstream `setsToWin = Math.ceil(1/2) = 1` and `isDecider = sets > 1 && ... = false`, so it silently behaves as a single set under a best-of label. (The quick-match equivalent correctly filters with `.filter(f => f.sets > 1)` at `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1825`.)
+
+User impact: Confusing/inconsistent state; a "best of" tournament configured to 1 set, labeled inconsistently. Not a wrong score, but a config trap.
+
+Suggested direction: Filter `setFormats.filter(f => f.sets > 1)` in the tournament best-of Sets picker, matching quick-match.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Single-set target stored under two different field names across engines (`target` vs `points`)
+
+Quick-match single: `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:363,1809,1867` write `format.target`; `:1023,1034` read `format.target`. Tournament single: `MonoTournamentSetup.jsx:1166` writes `{ type:'single', points:15 }`; `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:140,167` read `effectiveFormat.points`.
+
+What's wrong: The two scorers use different keys for the single-set target. Each path is internally consistent, but any shared helper, migration, or display that assumes one key will mis-read the other. `formatScoringDescription` (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:244`) defensively reads `format.target || format.points || ...`, which is evidence the codebase already knows the two coexist. A draft/resume crossing paths, or a future refactor, can read the wrong field and fall back to a default target.
+
+User impact: Latent — a single-set match whose format carries only `points` (tournament-shaped) loaded into a `target`-reading path would default to 15, changing the target. No confirmed user-visible break today.
+
+Suggested direction: Normalize on one field name (`points`) for the per-set target everywhere, or have `normalizeMatch` reconcile them.
+
+Confidence: medium.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Tournament scorer recomputes set/match completion locally instead of using the shared util
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:128-162` (`checkSetComplete`) duplicates `quickMatchSets.isSetComplete` / `getSetWinRule` with different precedence and different cap source.
+
+What's wrong: Two completion implementations exist for the same engine. They already disagree (badminton cap ordering — CRITICAL; volleyball standard cap source — HIGH). Any future rule change must be made in two places; the unit suite only tests one of them (`quickMatchSets.test.js`), leaving `checkSetComplete` unverified.
+
+User impact: Ongoing divergence risk; the same match scored in tournament vs quick-match can end differently at boundaries.
+
+Suggested direction: Replace `checkSetComplete` with `getSetWinRule` + `isSetComplete` from `quickMatchSets.js` and add tests covering the tournament path.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Rally serve-rotation "deuce" detection uses single-set `points`, which can be undefined for best-of
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:164-171,180-189` (`getCurrentSetTarget` + `rotateServeAfterPoint`).
+
+What's wrong: `rotateServeAfterPoint` computes `atDeuce` using `getCurrentSetTarget`, which for `formatType==='single'` returns `format.points`. If a single-set tournament format arrives carrying `target` instead of `points` (see the field-name divergence above), `target` here is `undefined`, making `score >= target - 1` evaluate against `NaN` (always false) and the at-deuce serve swap silently never triggers for table-tennis (serviceRotation 2). For best-of it resolves correctly, so impact is narrow.
+
+User impact: For table-tennis (every-2-points service) in a single-set tournament with a `points`-less format, the deuce single-serve rule would not engage; the serve indicator would be wrong. Edge, but a visible correctness issue for the serve indicator.
+
+Suggested direction: Make `getCurrentSetTarget` fall back to `format.target` and `pointsPerSet` for the single case.
+
+Confidence: medium.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] "Set Won" toast shows the wrong set ordinal (off-by-one) and stale current set
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:668` — `{setWonTeam} wins Set {currentSet}!`.
+
+What's wrong: The toast renders `Set {currentSet}` (0-based) rather than `Set {currentSet + 1}`. When set 1 (index 0) completes, it reads "wins Set 0". Worse, `addPoint` increments `currentSet` to the next set before the toast is read (line 273), so on a mid-match set the displayed number can reflect the already-advanced index. The badge elsewhere correctly uses `currentSet + 1` (line 507).
+
+User impact: Cosmetic but visibly wrong set number in the celebratory toast.
+
+Suggested direction: Capture the completed set index and render `+ 1`.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Hardcoded legacy blue `#0066ff` accents in the sets scorer violate the green design system
+
+`src/designs/design1-mono/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:498-499,558,590,656`.
+
+What's wrong: Swap-active border/text, the SERVE indicator, and the Save-Draft button use `#0066ff`, the dead blue accent that the project memory says was replaced by field green (`var(--primary)`). These should use the CSS token.
+
+User impact: Visual inconsistency with the rest of the Mono green theme.
+
+Suggested direction: Replace `#0066ff` with `var(--primary)`.
+
+Confidence: high.
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Single-set badminton has no 30-point cap (and best-of/single-set caps diverge)
+
+`src/utils/volleyballCalculations.js:13-21` (`validateSingleSetScore` takes no `maxPoints`), reached from `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1034` for single-set badminton.
+
+What's wrong: `validateSingleSetScore` has no cap parameter, so a single-game badminton match ignores the 30-cap entirely (it would require win-by-2 indefinitely — and per the CRITICAL bug above it actually ends at +1, so the cap question is partly moot until that is fixed). Either way, single-set and best-of badminton apply different cap rules.
+
+User impact: Single-game badminton does not honor the BWF 30 cap. Low because single-game badminton is uncommon and the dominant single-set defect is the win-by-2 bug.
+
+Suggested direction: Once win-by-2 is fixed, also thread `maxPoints` into the single-set rule for badminton.
+
+Confidence: medium.
