+# Score Easy — Runtime Testing Findings
+
+Hands-on testing of the **running app** (Vite dev server, web at desktop + mobile viewport, guest/signed-out).
+This complements the static code audit. Environment caveat: the preview tab reports `document.hidden = true`,
+so any visibility-/rAF-gated behaviour (match timers) could not be exercised, and `preview_screenshot` capture
+timed out repeatedly (environment limitation, **not** an app bug). All findings below are behavioural observations.
+
+## What works (verified end-to-end at runtime)
+
+- **All 4 scoring engines score correctly:**
+  - **Sets** (volleyball): point increment, set win, set→set progression, best-of-N match win, result screen, save.
+  - **Goals** (football): goals, End-Match confirm dialog, winner result, save. Basketball **+1/+2/+3** (verified +2 then +3 = 5), rugby **Penalty(3)/Try(5)/Try+Conv(7)/Drop(3)**, kabaddi **+1/Super Tackle(+2)/All Out(+2)** all render & register.
+  - **Cricket (limited overs):** 6 legal balls → 1.0 over; **Wide (+1)** adds a run without advancing the ball; wicket on next legal ball → **16/1 at 1.1 ov, RR 13.71** — all correct. Powerplay indicator shown.
+  - **Tennis (dedicated scorer):** point ladder **15 → 30 → 40** correct; **keyboard shortcuts (Q/P/U)** work; aria-live score announcement; per-set match grid.
+- **All 14 sports' setup screens mount** with correct rule summaries (table tennis Best of 5, timed sports 40/60/80/90 min, etc.).
+- **Save → History pipeline:** completed matches appear in History with sport/result/date/duration, filters, and counts. Abandoned 0-0 match correctly **not** saved.
+- **Statistics screen:** renders rich aggregates (top team, last-5 form, streak, head-to-head, closest/biggest match, draw rate, avg margin); overview counts correct (Matches 2, Teams 4 unique, Tournaments 0).
+- **Scoring-exit guard:** navigating away mid-match shows "Leave this page? Your unsaved scoring progress may be lost." Both branches work (Stay here / Leave page). In-progress match resumes after reload ("Resumed your in-progress quick match").
+- **Mobile viewport:** bottom nav (Play/History/Stats/Sign in), hamburger menu, desktop links hidden — responsive switch works.
+- **Tournament flow:** 4-step wizard (Basics→Rules→Teams→Review); **round-robin of 4 teams → 6 matches, all 6 pairings unique & complete**; schedule preview; match scorer mounts; **partial save** ("In Progress" / Resume); **destructive "Clear" confirms** before wiping.
+
+## Runtime issues found
+
+### R1 — Volleyball default format is wrong (Best of 3 instead of Best of 5) [HIGH]
+`sportRegistry.js` sets volleyball `defaultSetFormat: 2` (→ `setFormats[2]` = "Best of 5"), but the running app
+defaults volleyball to **"Best of 3 - 25 pts"** in BOTH quick match setup and tournament setup ("Format Best of 3 - 25 pts").
+Comparison: badminton (`defaultSetFormat: 1`) correctly shows "Best of 3", table tennis (`defaultSetFormat: 1`) correctly
+shows "Best of 5" — so the index→format mapping is being mis-applied specifically for volleyball's default. Users expecting
+the registry/marketing default ("Best of 5") get Best of 3. Evidence: `src/models/sportRegistry.js:22`; observed at `/volleyball/quick` and `/volleyball/tournament/new` review step.
+
+### R2 — Heavy re-render on every score action makes rapid scoring laggy [HIGH / perf]
+Each tap/score re-renders a very large component tree (+ a localStorage write). Measured throughput while driving:
+quick scorer ~1 action/sec; **tournament match scorer ~0.3 action/sec (~3s per point)** — 25 key-presses only registered
+9 before a 30s tool timeout. A best-of-3 volleyball match (~50 points) is impractically slow to tap out. Likely the 2,836-line
+`MonoQuickMatch.jsx` / tournament `MonoTournamentLiveScore` re-rendering wholesale per increment. (Corroborates the static performance audit.)
+
+### R3 — Tournament in-progress card shows a premature set tally [MEDIUM, verify]
+After scoring 9 points (set NOT complete) and "Save & Return", the Match 1 card reads **"Team 1 1 vs Team 2 0 · 9-0"** —
+i.e. it appears to show **1-0 in sets** when no set has been won (only 9 points in set 1). Either the set count is computed
+prematurely or the layout is misleading. Evidence: `/volleyball/tournament/:id` match card; component `MonoTournamentList`/`KnockoutMatchCard`. Needs code confirmation.
+
+### R4 — Two different scoring UIs for the same sport (quick vs tournament) [MEDIUM / UX consistency]
+Volleyball **quick** scorer = "Left side / Right side", serving indicator, Swap, no keyboard. Volleyball **tournament** scorer =
+"Tap to score", keyboard shortcuts (Q/P/U), aria-live, no serving/swap. Same sport, two materially different scoring interfaces —
+inconsistent muscle memory and feature parity (tournament lacks serving indicator; quick lacks keyboard).
+
+### R5 — "Resumed your in-progress match" banner is persistent [LOW / UX]
+The resume notice stays on screen through subsequent scoring and set changes; it never auto-dismisses and has no dismiss control.
+
+### R6 — Tennis setup uses "pts" instead of tennis terminology [LOW / copy]
+`/tennis/quick` rule summary reads "Best of 3 - **6 pts** - win by 2". Tennis is scored in **games** per set (registry even has
+`scoringLabel: 'games'`). "6 pts" is incorrect/confusing tennis terminology.
+
+### R7 — Cricket scorer exposes a "5" run button absent from registry config [LOW / drift]
+The live cricket scorer shows run buttons 0,1,2,3,**4,5,6** while `sportRegistry` cricket `quickButtons` lists 0,1,2,3,4,6,W
+(no 5). 5 runs is valid in cricket, so the UI is arguably more correct — but the registry/UI are out of sync.
+
+### R8 — `/play` category tabs: order + a single-item category [LOW / UX]
+Tab order (Cricket, Team, Net, Racquet, Contact) differs from `getSportsByCategory` order, and **"Net Sports" contains only volleyball** — a one-item category reads oddly.
+
+### R9 — Statistics tie-breaks resolve arbitrarily [LOW]
+With two 1-win teams and two 1-match sports, "Top team" and "Most played sport" pick one without an explicit, explained tie-break.
+
+## Needs on-device / focused-window verification (could not test in preview)
+- Match **timer ticking** (countdown for timed sports; stopwatch for volleyball) — preview tab is `hidden`, so visibility/rAF-gated timers stay frozen. Confirm the clock advances on a real device and pauses correctly on background.
+- Full tournament match **completion → standings/NRR/points update** — couldn't finish a match via UI due to R2 scoring lag.
+- Native Android: hardware back button, deep links, share sheet, splash, safe-area insets (Capacitor — code-audited only).
