+# Futsal — Per-Sport Audit
+
+## Summary
+
+The futsal config in `src/models/sportRegistry.js` (lines 312–342) is **essentially correct**. Engine (`goals`), scoring unit (`goal`), points model (3 win / 1 draw / 0 loss with `drawAllowed: true`), `standingsColumns` (P W D L GF GA GD Pts), and all `timePresets` second-values (600 / 1200 / 2400 = 10 / 20 / 40 min) are accurate for league futsal. The end-to-end flow was traced and works: `/play` (Team Sports) → `/futsal/quick` → goals setup (free / timed / points) → in-component goals scorer → finalize (draw correctly produces a "Draw" winner) → `persistQuickMatch` → `se_quickmatches` → appears in `MonoHistory` as "Futsal", draw filter included. Tournament standings pass `sportConfig.config` (3/1/0) into `calculateGoalsStandings`. No critical/high/medium issues found — only two low-severity polish items.
+
+**Severity tally:** critical 0 · high 0 · medium 0 · low 2
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Futsal shares the ⚽ emoji with Football in the quick-match header
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:315` — futsal `icon: '⚽'`
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:183` — football `icon: '⚽'` (identical)
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1393` — `{sportConfig?.icon || '🏐'} Quick Match` (header renders the emoji)
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1971` — `<span className="text-2xl">{sportConfig?.icon || '🏐'}</span>` (setup summary)
+
+**What's wrong:** Futsal and football carry the same `⚽` emoji in the registry. Whenever the registry `icon` field is rendered as an emoji — the quick-match header and setup summary — futsal is visually indistinguishable from football. Note the scope is narrow: the sport *picker* (`MonoSportHome.jsx:556`) renders a dedicated SVG via `<SportIcon name={sport.name} />`, and there genuinely is a distinct `FutsalIcon` (an indoor-court/goal glyph, `src/designs/design1-mono/landing/sportIcons.jsx:91`, mapped at line 252) that differs from `FootballIcon` (a soccer ball, line 81). `MonoHistory` rows use the text sport name, not the emoji. So the only place the duplicate shows is the quick-match header/summary.
+
+**User impact:** Minor visual ambiguity on the futsal Quick Match screen — the header emoji looks like football. Low because the dominant futsal surfaces (picker, history) already disambiguate.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Either give futsal a distinct emoji in the registry (no single perfect glyph exists; `🥅` goal or `🏟️` could read as "indoor"), or have the quick-match header render the SVG `SportIcon` by name (as the picker does) instead of the registry emoji, so it picks up the distinct `FutsalIcon`.
+
+**Confidence:** high (verified the emoji is used at MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1393/1971 and that picker/history do not use it).
+
+---
+
+### [LOW] Marketing bullets claim "Indoor 5v5" but the app cannot represent a roster / player count for goals sports
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:317` — `desc: 'Indoor football, 5v5'`
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:336–341` — `features: ['Indoor 5v5', '3 points for a win', 'Goal difference', 'Fast-paced matches']`
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1880–1948` — the `isGoals` setup block offers only How-are-you-playing (free / timed / points), time limit, and "first to" — **no players-per-side control**.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1653–1685` — the "Players per side" control (with "wickets to bowl a team out" copy) is cricket-only, not reachable for goals sports.
+
+**What's wrong:** Futsal markets "5v5" / "Indoor 5v5", but the goals engine has no concept of team size — futsal matches are scored purely as two running goal tallies. Unlike kabaddi (`maxPlayers: 7`, line 362) the futsal config does not even set `maxPlayers`, and even if it did, nothing in the goals setup consumes it. So "5v5" is purely descriptive copy the product never enforces or displays.
