+# Handball — Per-Sport Audit
+
+## Summary
+
+The handball config in `sportRegistry.js` is **substantially correct**. Unlike football/futsal/hockey (which use FIFA-style 3-points-for-a-win), handball correctly uses the IHF/EHF **2-1-0** league points (`winPoints:2 / drawPoints:1 / lossPoints:0`), and the standings calculator consumes these values faithfully. Time presets (1800s=30min half, 3600s=60min full), `drawAllowed:true`, `scoringUnit:'goal'`, the unique 🤾 icon, the `quickButtons:null` → single "+1" fallback, and goals-engine routing (quick + tournament) are all verified correct for handball. The findings below are one medium display defect (shared across goals sports, but handball is the most absurd instance because its win-target fallback is 2) and two low-severity polish/consistency items. No critical or high issues.
+
+Severity tally: **critical 0, high 0, medium 1, low 2.**
+
+### [MEDIUM] "By points" mode with no target chosen shows "First to 2 goals" for handball
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:250` — `return \`First to ${format.target || sportConfig?.config?.winPoints || 5} ${sportConfig?.config?.scoringUnit || 'point'}s\`;`. Reached via the format step: clicking "By points" runs `setFormat({ mode: opt.key })` (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1895`) which sets `mode:'points'` with **no `target`**; the point presets are only applied if the user taps one (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1938`). The "Next: Teams" button (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1954`) has no guard requiring a target, so a user can advance with `format.target` undefined. The summary renders on the Teams step at `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1980` via `ruleSummary` (`getRuleSummary`, `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:229`).
+- **What's wrong:** When `format.target` is falsy, the summary falls back to `sportConfig.config.winPoints`. For handball `winPoints:2`, so the rules summary reads **"First to 2 goals"** — a nonsensical target for a sport whose real full-time scores are ~25-35 per side. Worse, the scorer's win-on-target check is `if ((formatMode||'free')==='points' && effectiveFormat.target)` (`scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:222`), so with no target the match never actually auto-ends at 2 — the summary promises a stop condition that won't fire.
+- **User impact:** A handball user who picks "By points" and forgets to tap a preset sees "First to 2 goals," then the match never ends at 2. Misleading and confusing. Handball is the single worst-looking instance of this shared bug (winPoints=2 is the smallest among goals sports; football/hockey=3, basketball/cricket=2, rugby=4).
+- **Suggested direction:** Either (a) default a sensible target when "By points" is selected (e.g. seed `target` to the first `pointPresets` entry, 10 for handball), or (b) gate "Next: Teams" until a target is chosen in points mode, or (c) drop the `winPoints` fallback in `getRuleSummary` line 250 (winPoints is a *standings* value, never a match target). Note this is shared across all goals sports; flag to the shared-engine owner but handball is the most visible case.
+- **Confidence:** high (display path traced end-to-end; the only uncertainty is how often users skip the preset, which affects frequency not correctness).
+
+### [LOW] "2 halves format" feature bullet claims a format the timer engine does not implement
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:308` lists `'2 halves format'`; the timed mode is a single countdown — `if (formatMode==='timed' && timeLimit && timer.elapsed >= timeLimit)` (`scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:137`) — with no half-time break, no period/half boundary, and no per-half score tracking.
+- **What's wrong:** The marketing bullet advertises a "2 halves" structure, but the engine runs one flat timer (and the "30 min (Half)" preset is just a 30-minute single timer, not a structured half). The config is accurate against *real handball rules* but inconsistent with what the *app actually does*.
+- **User impact:** Minor expectation mismatch — a user expecting half-time handling won't get it. Cosmetic.
+- **Suggested direction:** Reword to something the engine delivers (e.g. "High-scoring, time-based") or implement period structure in the goals engine. Note this is the same class of overstatement as basketball's "Quarter tracking" (`sportRegistry.js:244`), but it lives in handball's own config entry so it is fair to report here.
+- **Confidence:** high.
+
+### [LOW] `pointPresets` (10/15/20/25) reflect recreational targets, not real handball scorelines
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:301` — `pointPresets: [10, 15, 20, 25]`. These surface in "By points" mode as "First to 10/15/20/25 goals" (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1935-1944`).
+- **What's wrong:** Real handball is time-based (2×30 min) with full-time totals typically 25-35 goals per team; a "first to 10" target ends a game well before a realistic handball scoreline. This is a legitimate casual/quick-play option, so it is not a bug — but the top preset (25) is the only one near a real final score, and there is no "30" option.
+- **User impact:** None functional; users wanting a realistic target only have "25" and nothing higher. Polish-level.
+- **Suggested direction:** Optional — consider presets like [15, 20, 25, 30] to better straddle casual and realistic handball, or leave as-is since "By time / 60 min (Full)" already covers the realistic format.
+- **Confidence:** medium (judgment call on realism, not a code defect).
+
+## Verified correct (no action needed)
+
+- **Standings points:** `winPoints:2 / drawPoints:1 / lossPoints:0` matches IHF/EHF handball (2-1-0). Consumed correctly by `src/utils/standingsCalculator.js:96,132-145` (and `drawAllowed:true` triggers the draw branch at line 141). `standingsColumns` `['P','W','D','L','GF','GA','GD','Pts']` is appropriate.
+- **Time presets:** `1800` = 30 min (one half) ✓, `3600` = 60 min (full match, 2×30) ✓, labels "30 min (Half)" / "60 min (Full)" accurate.
+- **Engine & flow:** `engine:'goals'` → quick match mounts `MonoGoalsLiveScore`; `quickButtons:null` correctly renders a single "+ 1" button (`scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:486-496`), which is right for handball (every goal = 1). Tournament routes to `GenericGoalsTournament` (`index.jsx:994-995`). Registry membership confirmed in `getSportsByCategory` Team Sports (`sportRegistry.js:474`), so `/play → MonoSportHome` selection is covered by the generic picker.
+- **Icon/identity:** 🤾 (`sportRegistry.js:283`) is unique across all 14 sports (verified — duplicates exist only for ⚽ football/futsal, 🎾 tennis/squash, 🏓 tabletennis/pickleball, none involving handball). Name "Handball" and `scoringUnit:'goal'` correct.
+
+## Deferred (shared-engine, not handball-scoped)
+
+- The goals scorer's scoring-button aria-labels say "point" (`scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:481,524,492,535`) even when `scoringUnit` is "goal". Affects all goals sports — defer to the shared-engine agent.
