+# Pickleball — Per-Sport Audit
+
+## Summary
+
+The pickleball config in `src/models/sportRegistry.js` (lines 123–150) and its standard defaults in `src/utils/sportDefaults.js` (lines 50–58) are mostly accurate: 11-point games, win-by-2, best-of-3, no point cap (matching traditional pickleball rules), and the setup→engine→save flow wires correctly through the shared sets engine. No critical or high-severity defects were found — score/result integrity is intact and the omission of a `maxPoints` cap is **correct** for pickleball, not a bug. The real issues are config-accuracy and content-consistency nits: `serviceRotation: 1` mismodels pickleball's side-out serve (flips the serve indicator every point in the default rally mode), an unrealistic single-game preset (`9` points; missing `21`), a features-vs-config mismatch, the shared 🏓 icon with table tennis, and "deuce"/"set" terminology that isn't native to pickleball.
+
+**Severity tally:** Critical 0 · High 0 · Medium 2 · Low 5
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] serviceRotation: 1 mismodels pickleball serve; serve indicator flips every point in default rally mode
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:141` (`serviceRotation: 1, // Rally scoring, service changes every point`); consumed in `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:174-178` (`if (rotation === 1) { setServingTeam(prev => prev === 1 ? 2 : 1); return; }`) and `:432` (`showServeIndicator = scoringMode === 'side-out' || Boolean(sportConfig?.config?.serviceRotation)`).
+- **What's wrong:** In pickleball the serve does **not** alternate every point — even under rally scoring. Serve changes on a side-out (the side that wins the rally / when the serving side faults gets/keeps the serve); a serving side that keeps winning keeps serving. `serviceRotation: 1` means "flip serve unconditionally every point," which is the badminton model, not pickleball. Because pickleball's `defaultScoringMode` is `'rally'` (registry:140), `showServeIndicator` is truthy via `Boolean(serviceRotation)` even in rally mode, so the on-court serve indicator renders and **toggles teams every single point** — misrepresenting who is serving. By contrast, squash — which has the same serve-follows-winner behavior — is correctly set to `serviceRotation: null` (registry:168), so squash shows no misleading indicator.
+- **User impact:** A pickleball scorer watching the serve indicator sees it bounce between teams every point, which contradicts how the serve actually moves. Cosmetic/informational only — it does not corrupt the score, set completion, or saved result.
+- **Suggested direction:** Set pickleball `serviceRotation: null` (mirroring squash) so the rally-mode serve indicator is suppressed, OR teach the shared engine a side-out-aware rotation for rally mode. The first is a one-line config fix you own; the engine-side rotation mechanics are shared-engine and deferred to the engine owner.
+- **Confidence:** high (config value and its consumption verified; behavior is the default rally experience).
+
+### [MEDIUM] Single-game preset includes unrealistic `9` and omits common `21`
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:135` — `{ label: 'Single game', sets: 1, points: [9, 11, 15] }`.
+- **What's wrong:** Pickleball is not played to 9 points; that target is not a recognized format. Common pickleball game targets are 11 (standard), 15, and 21 (longer/tournament games). The preset offers `9` (unrealistic) but is missing `21` (a real, frequently-used target). For comparison, table tennis offers `[7, 11, 21]` and volleyball `[10, 15, 21, 25]`.
+- **User impact:** A user picking a single-game pickleball match is offered a nonsensical "9 points" option and cannot one-tap a realistic 21-point game; minor confusion / extra friction (they can still custom-set it elsewhere).
+- **Suggested direction:** Change the preset to `[11, 15, 21]`.
+- **Confidence:** high.
+
+### [LOW] features bullet "Rally point scoring" understates the configured rally+side-out support
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:144-149` features lists only `'Rally point scoring'`, while config declares `scoringModes: ['rally', 'side-out']` (registry:139) and the landing card says `rules: 'rally or side-out'` (`src/designs/design1-mono/landing/landingData.js:15`).
+- **What's wrong:** The marketing `features` bullet advertises rally-only, but the sport actually supports both rally and side-out scoring (and the live scorer exposes a toggle — `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:435`). The features list is internally inconsistent with both the config and the landing copy.
+- **User impact:** Feature list undersells a capability the app has; trivial.
+- **Suggested direction:** Update the bullet to e.g. `'Rally or side-out scoring'`.
+- **Confidence:** high.
+
+### [LOW] Pickleball shares the 🏓 paddle icon with Table Tennis
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:126` (pickleball `icon: '🏓'`) and `:67` (tabletennis `icon: '🏓'`).
+- **What's wrong:** Two distinct sports use the identical emoji in the sport picker, history rows, and tournament screens. (Note: there is no dedicated pickleball emoji in Unicode, so this is a known constraint, but the duplicate still hurts at-a-glance distinction.)
+- **User impact:** In lists mixing both sports, users can't visually distinguish pickleball from table tennis by icon alone; they must read the label.
+- **Suggested direction:** Use a different glyph for one of them (e.g. a non-emoji SVG sport icon as already used elsewhere via `SportIcon`), or accept and rely on labels. Cross-sport concern — coordinate with the table-tennis auditor.
+- **Confidence:** high (duplicate confirmed).
+
+### [LOW] "Win by 2 at deuce" — "deuce" is not pickleball terminology
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:147` — features bullet `'Win by 2 at deuce'`.
+- **What's wrong:** "Deuce" is tennis/table-tennis vocabulary. Pickleball just says "win by 2"; there is no "deuce" call. (The same phrasing also appears in shared setup copy, e.g. `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2629` "Win by 2 at deuce", but that string is reused across sets sports.)
+- **User impact:** Minor terminology inaccuracy a pickleball player would notice.
+- **Suggested direction:** Reword pickleball's bullet to `'Win by 2 margin'` or simply `'Win by 2'`.
+- **Confidence:** medium (terminology judgment).
+
+### [LOW] Engine UI labels matches as "Set N" rather than pickleball "games"
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:507` (`Set ${currentSet + 1} of ${effectiveFormat.sets}`), `:617` (`Set {i + 1}: …`), `:668` (`wins Set {currentSet}!`). Pickleball config / features correctly use "games" (registry:135 label `'Single game'`, :145 `'Best of 3 games to 11'`).
+- **What's wrong:** Pickleball segments are "games," not "sets." The shared sets scorer hardcodes "Set", so a live pickleball match shows "Set 1 of 3" / "wins Set 1" rather than "Game 1 of 3." This contradicts the sport's own config wording.
+- **User impact:** Terminology mismatch during live scoring; non-blocking.
+- **Suggested direction:** Drive the segment noun from a per-sport label (badminton/TT/squash already say "games" too), e.g. a `scoringLabel`/`segmentLabel` config key consumed by the scorer. This is sets-engine-wide (affects badminton, table tennis, squash equally), so it is **deferred to the shared-engine owner** — noted here only because it surfaces visibly for pickleball.
+- **Confidence:** high (labels confirmed; correctly scoped as shared-engine).
+
+### [LOW] Standard pickleball default carries no scoringMode (relies on scorer fallback)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/utils/sportDefaults.js:50-58` pickleball default omits any `scoringMode`; the scorer falls back to `defaultScoringMode` via `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:91-100`.
+- **What's wrong:** The standard-mode format object for pickleball doesn't explicitly carry `scoringMode: 'rally'`, so the live mode is resolved only by the scorer's fallback chain. It currently lands on `'rally'` correctly (registry `defaultScoringMode: 'rally'` is in `scoringModes`), so there is **no live defect** — but the default is implicit rather than explicit, making it fragile if the fallback logic changes.
+- **User impact:** None today; latent maintainability risk only.
+- **Suggested direction:** Optionally add `scoringMode: 'rally'` to the pickleball `sportDefaults` entry for explicitness. Low priority.
+- **Confidence:** medium.
+
+---
+
+## Explicitly verified as correct (no action)
+
+- **No `maxPoints` cap** for pickleball (registry has none; `sportDefaults.js:55-57` has no `pointCap`). This is **correct** — traditional pickleball is win-by-2 with no hard ceiling, unlike badminton (cap 30, registry:47) and volleyball (cap 27, sportDefaults:12). The cap logic at `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:143/159` and `quickMatchSets.js:41` is simply not triggered for pickleball, which is the intended behavior.
+- **`pointsPerSet: 11`, `deciderPoints: 11`, `winBy: 2`, `defaultSetFormat: 1` (Best of 3)** all match real pickleball and are consumed correctly (target resolution at `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:148-150`, win check at `:155-159`).
+- **Standard defaults** (`sportDefaults.js:50-58`): best-of-3, 11 points, win-by-2 — accurate.
+- **Side-out serve handling** (`MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:220-223`, gated `scoringMode !== 'side-out'` at `:229-231`) is correct; serve stays with the server in side-out mode.
+- **standingsColumns** `['P','W','L','GW','GL','PF','PA','+/-','Pts']` (registry:143) — uses "GW/GL" (games won/lost), consistent with the sport's "games" framing; matches the sets-sport pattern (badminton/TT/squash identical).
+- **Category placement** — pickleball under "Racquet Sports" (`getSportsByCategory`, registry:462-469) is correct.
