+# Rugby
+
+## Summary
+
+The rugby config in `src/models/sportRegistry.js` (lines 380-416) is mostly accurate to real Rugby Union: try (5), conversion (2), penalty (3), drop goal (3), the 7 = try+conversion math, league points (4 win / 2 draw / 0 loss), the 80-minute standard timed default, and the time presets are all correct. However, rugby is the **only** sport that declares `bonusPoints: true` and the **only** goals sport whose `standingsColumns` has 9 entries (it adds `BP`). Both of those promises are unfulfilled: the bonus-point system is never implemented anywhere in the codebase, and the extra `BP` column desynchronizes the tournament standings table header from its fixed body cells — so in every rugby tournament the points value renders under the `BP` header and the final `Pts` column renders empty. Net: 0 critical, 2 high, 1 medium, 2 low. Scoring math and the quick-match save→history path are correct.
+
+Severity tally: critical 0 · high 2 · medium 1 · low 2
+
+### [HIGH] Rugby standings table: header/body column mismatch mislabels the points value and leaves `Pts` empty
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:409` — `standingsColumns: ['P', 'W', 'D', 'L', 'PF', 'PA', '+/-', 'BP', 'Pts']` (9 entries). `src/designs/design1-mono/GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:370-372` renders one `<th>` per `standingsColumns` entry (9 headers + the `#`/`Team` headers). But the body `src/designs/design1-mono/GenericGoalsTournament.jsx:380-392` renders a **fixed** set of `<td>` cells: played, won, (drawn only if `drawAllowed`), lost, goalsFor, goalsAgainst, goalDiff, points — 8 data cells for rugby (D is shown because rugby has `drawAllowed: true`).
+- **What's wrong:** Header has 9 stat columns, body has only 8 stat cells. Columns align correctly through `+/-`, then the **points number lands under the `BP` header** and the final **`Pts` column has no cell and renders empty**. Every other goals sport matches (football 8 header/8 body, basketball 7/7, kabaddi 8/8) — rugby is the sole sport whose column counts disagree, because of the extra `BP`.
+- **User impact:** In any rugby tournament, the standings table shows the league-points total under a "BP" label and an empty "Pts" column. The single most important number in the table is mislabeled. High confusion; users cannot trust the table.
+- **Suggested direction:** Either (a) remove `'BP'` from rugby's `standingsColumns` until bonus points are implemented, or (b) implement bonus points (see next finding) and add a matching `<td>` for `BP` in `GenericGoalsTournament.jsx`. The fix touches shared display/config code, but rugby is the only sport that triggers it.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [HIGH] `bonusPoints: true` is declared but the bonus-point system is never implemented; standings ignore it
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:400` — `bonusPoints: true`. The standings engine `src/utils/standingsCalculator.js:96` destructures only `{ winPoints, drawPoints, lossPoints, drawAllowed }` from config — `bonusPoints` is never read. The stats object (`standingsCalculator.js:98-109`) has no bonus field, and points are computed solely from win/draw/loss (`standingsCalculator.js:132-145`). A repo-wide search for `bonusPoints`/`BP` outside the registry/config and docs finds no consuming logic.
+- **What's wrong:** Rugby Union league tables award bonus points (e.g., 4 tries scored, or losing by ≤7) on top of the 4/2/0 base. The config advertises this (`bonusPoints: true`, the `BP` column, and the feature bullet "Bonus point system" at `src/models/sportRegistry.js:413`), but nothing computes or stores bonus points. Standings points are just 4×wins + 2×draws.
+- **User impact:** Rugby tournament standings are incomplete versus what the app advertises. A real rugby competition's ladder would differ from what Score Easy shows. The "Bonus point system" marketing bullet is false.
+- **Suggested direction:** Either implement bonus-point capture (needs per-match try counts / losing margin, which the goals scorer does not currently track) plus a `BP` column in the standings table, or remove `bonusPoints: true`, the `BP` column, and the "Bonus point system" feature bullet so config matches behavior. Lean toward implementing or honestly removing — do not leave the advertised-but-absent state.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [MEDIUM] "Bonus point system" feature bullet advertises an unimplemented feature
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:410-415` — features include `'Bonus point system'`. As established above, no bonus-point logic exists in `standingsCalculator.js` or anywhere else.
+- **What's wrong:** The marketing/feature bullet (surfaced on the sport picker and rule summaries) claims a capability the app does not have. The task explicitly asks whether feature bullets are accurate and consistent with config — this one is not.
+- **User impact:** Misleading expectation. A user choosing rugby for its bonus-point ladder will not get one.
+- **Suggested direction:** Remove the bullet (and ideally pair it with resolving the two findings above), or implement the feature. Tracked separately because the task calls out feature-bullet accuracy; can be folded into the bonus-points fix.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [LOW] Points-mode auto-end can overshoot the target with multi-value quick buttons
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1195-1199` (quick match) and `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoGoalsLiveScore.jsx:222-223` (tournament) end the match when `newScore >= format.target`. Rugby quick buttons add 3/5/7 (`src/models/sportRegistry.js:394-399`).
+- **What's wrong:** In opt-in custom "points" mode (first-to-N), a team at e.g. 18 pressing "Try+Conv (7)" jumps to 25 and the match records 25 vs. a 21 target. This is cosmetic — the final score is still recorded accurately, and points mode is a deliberate custom choice (standard rugby is timed). Real rugby is not first-to-N at all, so points mode is an unusual fit but not wrong.
+- **User impact:** Minor — a tournament/quick match in points mode may finish a few points above target. No data loss, no crash.
+- **Suggested direction:** Acceptable as-is; if desired, cap the recorded score at the target or document that points mode allows overshoot. Low priority.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+### [LOW] Icon usage — rugby is fine; note shared duplicates elsewhere (out of scope)
+
+- **Evidence:** `src/models/sportRegistry.js:383` — rugby uses `🏉` (unique). For contrast: squash (`:155`) and tennis (`:95`) both use `🎾`; pickleball (`:126`) and tabletennis (`:67`) both use `🏓`.
+- **What's wrong:** Rugby's icon and emoji are correct and unique — no issue. The duplicate-emoji concern flagged in the task applies to other sports (squash/tennis, pickleball/tabletennis), not rugby. Noted here only to show the check was performed; defer to those sports' auditors.
+- **User impact:** None for rugby.
+- **Suggested direction:** No action for rugby. Duplicates belong to the squash/tennis and pickleball/tabletennis audits.
+- **Confidence:** high
+
+## Verified correct (no issue)
+
+- **Scoring values:** try 5, conversion +2, penalty 3, drop goal 3, and "Try+Conv (7)" = 5+2 are all correct Rugby Union values (`src/models/sportRegistry.js:394-399`).
+- **League points:** win 4 / draw 2 / loss 0 (`src/models/sportRegistry.js:391-393`) match standard rugby competition points; consumed correctly by `standingsCalculator.js:96`.
+- **Standard timed default:** 80 minutes / 4800s (`src/utils/sportDefaults.js:101-105`) is correct (2×40 min Rugby Union).
+- **Time presets:** 20 min/1200s, 40 min (Half)/2400s, 80 min (Full)/4800s (`src/models/sportRegistry.js:402-406`) — all seconds values correct.
+- **`drawAllowed: true`** is correct for rugby pool play.
+- **Setup→scorer→save→history flow:** `/play` → select rugby → `/rugby/quick` (`MonoQuickMatch` setup, `isGoals` branch) → quick buttons render (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:2456-2483`) → end → `endMatchGoals` → `finalizeGoalScore` → `finalizeMatch` → `persistQuickMatch` + `syncCompletedMatch` (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:642-658`). Multi-value quick buttons feed into the `score1`/`score2` totals; undo (`undoGoal`, `MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1202-1211`) correctly subtracts `last.value` (e.g., removes a full 5 for a try). The save→appears-in-history path is the shared quick-match path used by all goals sports and works for rugby.
