+# Table Tennis — Per-Sport Audit
+
+## Summary
+
+Table tennis is configured on the shared **sets** engine. Its core scoring rules are **correct**: 11 points per game (`pointsPerSet: 11`), win-by-2 at deuce (`winBy: 2`), no point cap (TT has no cap, unlike badminton's 30), decider games also to 11 (`deciderPoints: 11`), Best-of-5 default, and service rotation every 2 points (`serviceRotation: 2`) — I simulated the rotation logic and it correctly alternates 2 serves each and switches every point at deuce (10-10+). All four `features` marketing bullets are accurate and consistent with the config, and `standingsColumns` correctly use GW/GL (games), not sets. The real issues are around the **custom-setup UI and terminology**, not the math. The most material defect: the standard TT value **11 is not in the global "Points per set" preset list** offered in custom mode, so a user customizing a TT match cannot pick 11 from the presets and sees nothing highlighted. Secondary: the live scorer and setup hardcode "Set"/"Points per set" even though TT is officially played in *games* (and the app's own config/features/standings call them games), the registry `icon` emoji 🏓 is shared with pickleball, and two registry fields (`defaultSetFormat`, the per-format `points` arrays) are dead config.
+
+**Severity tally:** Critical 0 · High 0 · Medium 3 · Low 3
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] "Points per set" presets omit 11 — TT's defining value is not selectable in custom mode
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1842-1852` — the "Points per set" buttons render `POINTS_PRESETS.map(...)`.
+- `src/utils/volleyballCalculations.js:91-96` — `POINTS_PRESETS = [10, 15, 21, 25]`. **11 is absent.**
+- `src/utils/sportDefaults.js:28-36` — TT standard default is `points: 11`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1481` — the "Custom" button only calls `setFormatMode('custom')` and does NOT reset `format`, so `format.points` stays 11.
+
+**What's wrong:** In standard mode TT correctly plays to 11. But when a user picks **Custom** → step 2 "Points per set", the only presets are 10/15/21/25. The active value (11) matches no button, so **no button is highlighted** and the user cannot re-select 11 if they tap away. The same gap hits the Single-set custom path: `setFormat(... target: prev.target || 15 ...)` (`MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1809`) defaults to 15 and offers the same 4 presets — 11 is unreachable there too.
+
+**User impact:** A table-tennis player customizing a match is presented with a points-per-game list that excludes the one value that defines the sport, and the default state looks "nothing selected." Confusing and slightly broken; the standard path saves them, so it is not a hard failure.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Source the per-set point presets from the sport's `setFormats[…].points` (TT already declares `[7, 11, 21]`) instead of the global volleyball `POINTS_PRESETS`, or add 11 to the shared preset list. (Shared-setup file — affects badminton/squash/pickleball, all of which use 11/21, similarly.)
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Live scorer & setup label TT games as "Sets" / "Points per set" — contradicts the sport's own config
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:83` — TT `standingsColumns: ['P','W','L','GW','GL',...]` (Games Won/Lost).
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:84-89` — features say "Best of 5 or 7 **games**", "11 points per **game**".
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx:507` — header renders `Set ${currentSet + 1} of ${effectiveFormat.sets}`; `:452/:455` show "Set complete"; `:531` aria text "Set N of M".
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1822` ("Sets" label) and `:1840` ("Points per set").
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:111` — `scoringLabel: 'games'` exists ONLY for tennis and is never read by the sets scorer (grep shows no consumption in `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx`).
+
+**What's wrong:** Table tennis is officially played in **games** (best-of-5/7 games to 11 points). The registry agrees with itself (GW/GL columns, "games" in features), but every live/setup string the user sees says "Set". There is a `scoringLabel` mechanism but it is (a) only set on tennis and (b) not actually consumed by the shared sets scorer.
+
+**User impact:** Terminology mismatch — a TT user sees "Set 1 of 5" / "Points per set" while the history/standings call them games. Internally inconsistent; not blocking.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Add `scoringLabel: 'games'` to TT (and badminton/squash/pickleball) and have `MonoSetsLiveScore.jsx` + the setup labels honor it (fallback to "Set"). Or standardize on "Game" for all racquet sets sports. Shared-engine surface — note and defer the rendering change to the engine owner; the missing `scoringLabel` on the TT config is in-scope.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Per-format `points` arrays in `setFormats` are dead config (TT "Single game" advertises 7/11/21 but UI ignores it)
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:76` — TT `setFormats[0] = { label: 'Single game', sets: 1, points: [7, 11, 21] }`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1825` — the Sets buttons map `setFormats.filter(f => f.sets > 1)` and read only `formatOption.label`/`.sets`; the `points` array is never referenced.
