+# Tennis — per-sport audit
+
+## Summary
+
+The tennis config in `sportRegistry.js` is mostly accurate for real tennis (games-to-6, win-by-2, tiebreak at 6-6 to 7, best-of-3 default), and the dedicated quick-match scorer (`MonoTennisLiveScore`) implements deuce/advantage, tiebreak, and set/match completion correctly. However tennis is the one sets-sport with its OWN scorer and its OWN per-set data shape (`games1`/`games2`, no `score1`/`score2`), and that shape silently breaks the shared sets-tournament UI and standings — a critical, untested integration gap. The custom-rules setup path is also effectively broken for tennis: it shows volleyball point presets (10/15/21/25) and a "Single set" option, none of which the tennis scorer honors, so user choices are silently ignored. The passing unit suite does not catch these because the standings tests feed the calculator volleyball-shaped (`score1/score2`) sets, never the tennis `games1/games2` shape that the tennis scorer actually persists.
+
+Severity tally: critical 1, high 3, medium 2, low 3.
+
+Verified correct (no issue): the `/play` → tennis tile and "Start Tennis" CTA (`startActions.js`, `MonoSportHome.jsx`) behave like every sets sport; the tennis QUICK-match → `/history` path renders correctly because `buildTennisQuickHistoryEntry` + `mapTennisSetsForQuickHistory` translate `games1/games2` → `score1/score2` and store explicit `setsWon1/2`; tennis tournaments correctly route to `MonoTennisLiveScore` (not the generic sets scorer) via `MonoTournamentLiveScore.jsx:30-31`; the deuce/advantage and tiebreak completion math in the scorer is sound and matches real rules.
+
+---
+
+### [CRITICAL] Tennis tournament sets persist as `games1/games2`, but standings + tournament UI read `score1/score2` — standings and match scores break
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:56-67` — `makeBlankSet()` produces `{ games1, games2, points1, points2, tiebreakPoints1, tiebreakPoints2, isTiebreak, completed }`. There is no `score1`/`score2` field.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:522-534` — tournament `saveMatch` persists `sets` raw (no remapping to `score1/score2`).
+- `src/utils/standingsCalculator.js:42-50` — `calculateSetsStandings` counts set wins with `set.score1 > set.score2` and accumulates `pointsFor/pointsAgainst` from `set.score1/score2`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/GenericSetsTournament.jsx:34-35, 242-243, 316, 321, 329-331` — match-completion repair, per-match set tallies, and per-set score rendering all read `set.score1/score2`.
+
+**What's wrong:** Tennis is the only sets sport whose dedicated scorer writes `games1/games2` instead of `score1/score2`. The quick path translates this shape via `mapTennisSetsForQuickHistory` (`tennisQuickMatch.js:10-21`), but the tournament save path does not. For tennis tournament matches, `set.score1`/`set.score2` are `undefined`, so `undefined > undefined` is `false` for every set: both teams register 0 sets won, no winner is derived in standings, no W/L/match-points accrue, and `pointsFor/pointsAgainst` accumulate `0`. The per-set score cells render `undefined-undefined`.
+
+**User impact:** A tennis tournament's standings table stays empty/zero no matter how many matches are played, and individual match scores display blank. The match itself still records a `winner` (the scorer computes it from `games`/tiebreak in `saveMatch`), so the result is saved — but the league table and score display are broken. This is a core-flow failure a user running a tennis tournament would immediately notice.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Tennis's dedicated scorer should emit the shared per-set contract (`score1/score2`) on tournament save, mirroring `mapTennisSetsForQuickHistory` (and folding in the tiebreak-winner fix below so a tiebreak set isn't a 6-6 tie). Defer to the engine agent only the orthogonal question of whether `calculateSetsStandings` should be defensive about set shape.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Tiebreak-won sets are never recorded in `games`, so the set score shows 6-6 (and counts as a tie in standings)
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:155-168` — `processTiebreakPoint` increments `tiebreakPoints1/2` and marks the set `completed`, but never bumps `games1`/`games2`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:708-710` — a completed tiebreak set renders as `${games1}-${games2} (${tb1}-${tb2})`, i.e. `6-6 (7-5)` instead of the tennis-correct `7-6 (7-5)`.
+
+**What's wrong:** In real tennis the tiebreak winner is awarded the 7th game, making the set 7-6. Here the set stays 6-6 in games. The scorer's own winner logic survives because `countSetsWon`/`isSetComplete` special-case `isTiebreak` (lines 75-83, 91-98), and quick history stores explicit `setsWon1/2`. But any consumer that infers the set winner from games (the tournament standings/UI in the CRITICAL finding, and the "6-6" set display itself) is wrong.
+
+**User impact:** Tiebreak sets display as 6-6 with the tiebreak in parentheses — confusing and non-standard. It also compounds the tournament-standings bug: even after a games→score remap, a 6-6 tiebreak set is a tie (0 sets won for both), so the standings fix is incomplete unless the tiebreak winner is reflected as 7-6.
+
+**Suggested direction:** On tiebreak completion, award the winning side the 7th game (set 7-6) so both the display and any games-derived winner inference are correct.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Custom-rules "Points per set" shows volleyball presets (10/15/21/25) that the tennis scorer ignores
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1843, 1864` — the sets custom-rules UI maps `POINTS_PRESETS`.
+- `src/utils/volleyballCalculations.js:91-96` — `POINTS_PRESETS = [10, 15, 21, 25] pts`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:74-84, 139-152, 179-190` — game/set/tiebreak thresholds are hardcoded (game at 4 points win-by-2, set at 6 games win-by-2, tiebreak at 6-6 to 7). `format.points` is never read by the tennis scorer.
+
+**What's wrong:** When a tennis user picks "Custom" → "Best-of", they are offered "10/15/21/25 pts" per set, which is meaningless for tennis (a set is games-to-6, not points-to-N). Worse, whatever they pick is silently discarded: the tennis scorer hardcodes 6 games / 7-point tiebreak. The config also declares `scoringLabel: 'games'` (`sportRegistry.js:111`) precisely to distinguish this, but the setup UI never consults it.
+
+**User impact:** The custom "Points per set" control is a no-op dead end for tennis — it implies configurability that doesn't exist and uses the wrong unit/values. Users who set "21 pts" still get a games-to-6 match with no warning.
+
+**Suggested direction:** For tennis, hide the "Points per set" control (or replace it with games/tiebreak options the scorer actually honors), or honor the chosen values in the scorer. At minimum, don't surface volleyball point values for tennis.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [HIGH] Custom "Single set" for tennis passes no `sets`, silently producing a best-of-3 match
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:1808-1814` — the "Single set" button sets `{ type: 'single', target: 15, points: 25 }` with no `sets` field.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:777-794` — tennis start passes `format` straight into `buildTennisQuickDraft`; it does not branch on `format.type === 'single'`.
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/scoring/MonoTennisLiveScore.jsx:302` — `buildInitialSets(draft.format?.sets || config.config?.sets || 3)`. Tennis config has no top-level `sets` key (`sportRegistry.js:92-121`), so a single-set tennis match falls back to 3 sets.
+
+**What's wrong:** Choosing "Single set" for tennis does not produce a single set. `format.sets` is undefined and the tennis config exposes no `sets` fallback, so the scorer builds a best-of-3 match. `isMatchComplete` (line 334-339) then requires 2 sets to win. The config's `setFormats` does define a `{ label: 'Single set', sets: 1, points: [4, 6] }` (`sportRegistry.js:106`), but the custom UI's "Single set" button doesn't use it and the standard path never offers it.
+
+**User impact:** A user who explicitly selects a one-set tennis match gets a best-of-3 instead — a clear functional defect; the match won't end when they expect.
+
+**Suggested direction:** Have the "Single set" button set `sets: 1` for sets sports (or read from the chosen `setFormats` entry), and/or give tennis a top-level `sets` fallback. Ensure `isMatchComplete` resolves to 1 set to win for single-set tennis.
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Rule summary labels tennis games as "pts" and ignores `scoringLabel: 'games'`
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/designs/design1-mono/MonoQuickMatch.jsx:241-244` — `getRuleSummary` sets branch returns `Best of ${sets} - ${points} pts - win by ${winBy}`, hardcoding the unit "pts".
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:111` — tennis declares `scoringLabel: 'games'`, which is never consulted by `getRuleSummary`.
+
+**What's wrong:** For standard tennis the summary reads "Best of 3 - 6 pts - win by 2". In tennis a set is 6 *games*, and "win by 2" reads as a points rule. The config has the correct label (`games`) but the summary ignores it.
+
+**User impact:** The match-rules summary on the Teams step mislabels tennis units, which looks unprofessional and is mildly confusing (6 "pts" implies points-to-6 scoring).
+
+**Suggested direction:** Use `sportConfig.config.scoringLabel` (falling back to "pts") when building the sets summary, and phrase tennis as games/sets rather than "pts".
+
+**Confidence:** high
+
+---
+
+### [MEDIUM] Tennis and squash share the 🎾 icon; pickleball and table tennis share 🏓
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:95` — tennis `icon: '🎾'`.
+- `src/models/sportRegistry.js:155` — squash `icon: '🎾'` (same ball).
